:\"https://kenh14.vn/home.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Kenh14\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=kenh14.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Entertainment\",\"title\":\"3 tính năng của Google Maps mà người chạy xe điện nên biết\",\"link\":\"https://kenh14.vn/3-tinh-nang-cua-google-maps-ma-nguoi-chay-xe-dien-nen-biet-215260723153325103.chn\",\"image\":\"https://kenh14cdn.com/zoom/600_315/203336854389633024/2026/7/23/avatar1784795518519-17847955189951489582724.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:30:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Không chỉ là ứng dụng dẫn đường quen thuộc, Google Maps ngày càng trở thành trợ thủ đắc lực của người dùng xe điện.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Chase Sapphire Preferred vs. Reserve: Which Should You Get in 2026?\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/best-chase-sapphire-card-2026/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Chase-Sapphire-Preferred-Chase-Sapphire-Reserve-Upgraded-Points-LLC-3.jpeg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:30:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Although you can now carry the Chase Sapphire Reserve ® and the Chase Sapphire Preferred ®  Card simultaneously , one might be a better fit over the other, depending on your travel, lifestyle, and spending habits. I’ve held each travel card at different points in my life, but as each one has evolved, reevaluating which has been right for me has been key to optimizing my spending, benefits, earnings, and redemptions. In this post, I’ll compare the 2 personal Chase Sapphire cards to help you decide which is a better fit for you this year. Chase Sapphire Reserve Card vs. the Chase Sapphire Preferred Card The Chase Sapphire Reserve card is Chase’s most premium card, with a $795 annual fee and a collection of lifestyle and travel benefits that can help you offset it. Meanwhile, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card comes with fewer perks, though the ones it does come with have been newly revamped and can easily help you outweigh the $95 annual fee. Welcome Offer Right now, you can take advantage of this welcome offer on the Chase Sapphire Reserve card: Earn 100,000 bonus points after you spend $6,000 on purchases in the first 3 months from account opening. Meanwhile, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card currently has a higher-than-usual welcome offer: Earn 75,000 100,000 points after spending $5,000 on purchases in the first 3 months. As you can see, you can currently earn the same 100,000 bonus points from each card’s welcome offer, but the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is the winner here (at least until the elevated bonus offer ends), because the card has a lower spending threshold to reach the bonus and a significantly lower annual fee. However, Chase has officially notified us that the 100,000-point bonus offer on the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is ending soon , so you’ll want to pick it up before it’s too late. Hot Tip: Welcome offers , especially elevated ones, don’t last forever. If you see a higher offer, apply for the card ASAP to avoid missing out. Travel and Lifestyle Perks and Benefits Regardless of the amount of each card’s annual fee, the key to outweighing either fee is to utilize the benefits and perks. The Chase Sapphire Reserve card has a higher annual fee but also offers a wide array of benefits. In fact, we estimate the card offers more than $7,000 in value thanks to its over 40 benefits . For example, the card offers perks such as: $300 annual travel credit  Complimentary Priority Pass membership with access to more than 1,300 airport lounges worldwide (with 2 guests) Chase Sapphire Lounge access that includes the cardholder plus 2 guests, as well as access to select Air Canada lounges with 1 guest A complimentary subscription to Apple TV and Apple Music that’s valid when activated by June 22, 2027, a value of $288 annually $300 annually in monthly DoorDash promos and complimentary access to DashPass for a minimum of 1 year (activate by December 31, 2027) Complimentary IHG One Rewards Platinum Elite Status Up to $500 in credits annually with The Edit by Chase Travel Book a restaurant that is part of Sapphire Reserve Exclusive Tables and receive  up to $300 in annual dining credits. TSA PreCheck, Global Entry, or NEXUS credit of up to $120 every 4 years Up to $120 annually ( up to $10 monthly) in Lyft  credit when you use your Chase Sapphire Reserve card to pay for your ride (through September 30, 2027) A wide range of travel and spending protections The Chase Sapphire Lounges are some of the best lounges. Image Credit: Stella Shon If cardholders spend $75,000 annually, they unlock additional perks , including IHG One Rewards Diamond elite status, World of Hyatt Explorist status, Southwest Airlines A-List status, a $500 Southwest Airlines Chase Travel credit, and a $250 credit for the Shops at Chase. Meanwhile, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card has a selection of newly updated perks , which include: Get up to $100 in hotel credit on Chase Travel hotel bookings annually A complimentary 1-year Apple TV subscription (activate by December 31, 2026 ) Up to $120 toward  Global Entry ,  TSA PreCheck , or  NEXUS  every 4 years Complimentary subscription to DoorDash DashPass (activate by December 31, 2027) and $10 monthly ($120 annually) in DoorDash credits . A collection of purchase and travel protections , including the newly added emergency evacuation and transportation coverage It’s true that the Chase Sapphire Preferred card has fewer benefits, but that makes it infinitely easier to offset the lower annual fee. Just using the hotel credit alone could make the card worth having. We estimate the value of the card’s many benefits to be nearly $5,000 . The winner? We love that the Chase Sapphire Preferred card’s benefits make it easy to offset the annual fee, but we can’t ignore the sheer volume of perks the Chase Sapphire Reserve card offers. The card features some of the most generous lounge access of any credit card, allowing 2 guests per lounge visit (at a time when many cards are reducing guest access) and numerous statement credits. It’s true that you have to keep track of more benefits, but the high value of these benefits definitely makes the Chase Sapphire Reserve card the winner in this category. Points Earnings Both cards earn Chase Ultimate Rewards points , a valuable, flexible rewards currency. The Chase Sapphire Reserve card offers the ability to earn big in specific categories: 8x points on all Chase Travel purchases 5x points on Lyft rides (through September 30, 2027) 4x points on flights and hotels booked directly 3x points on all dining purchases worldwide 1x points on everything else On the other hand, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card features the following spending bonus categories: 5x points on all travel booked via the Chase Travel portal 3x points on dining purchases, online grocery purchases (excluding Walmart, Target, and wholesale clubs), gas, EV charging, vacation homes (such as Airbnb and Vrbo), and some streaming services 2x points on all other travel worldwide 1x points on everything else While we appreciate the ability to earn more points with the big bonus categories on the Chase Sapphire Reserve card, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is the real winner when it comes to earnings . Why? Because the bonus categories are for things that many people tend to buy often. For example, I rarely spend on Lyft or in Chase Travel, but gas, general travel, and streaming are regular, frequent purchases for me. When you’re getting bonus points for regular, everyday purchases, it’s easier to accrue more points. Redemptions Both personal Sapphire cards make it easy for cardholders to redeem their Ultimate Rewards points , whether that’s for purchases in Chase Travel or for transferring points to airline and hotel partners. Below, you can see a list of Chase’s airline and hotel partners, which is the same for both the Chase Sapphire Reserve card and the Chase Sapphire Preferred card. SCROLL FOR MORE Chase Transfer Partner Minimum Transfer Transfer Ratio Transfer Time Airline Programs Aer Lingus AerClub 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant Air Canada Aeroplan 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant Air France-KLM Flying Blue 1,000 1:1 1 hour The British Airways Club 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant Club Iberia Plus 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant JetBlue TrueBlue 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant Singapore Airlines KrisFlyer 1,000 1:1 1 to 2 days Southwest Airlines Rapid Rewards 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant United Airlines MileagePlus 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant Virgin Atlantic Flying Club 1,000 1:1 Almost Instant Hotel Programs IHG One Rewards 1,000 1:1 1 day Marriott Bonvoy 1,000 1:1 2 days World of Hyatt 1,000 1:1* Almost Instant Wyndham Rewards 1,000 1:1 1 to 7 business days * Chase Sapphire Preferred® Card and Ink Business Preferred® Credit Card cardmembers’ Ultimate Rewards points will transfer to World of Hyatt at a rate of 4:3. This is effective immediately for new Chase Sapphire Preferred cardmembers who apply on or after June 15, 2026, and effective October 1, 2026, for cardmembers who applied prior to June 15, 2026. For Ink Business Preferred cardmembers, this is effective October 1, 2026, for existing cardmembers and for new cardmembers who apply on or after October 1, 2026. However, there’s one major difference that makes the Chase Sapphire Reserve card win in this category: the transfer ratio to Hyatt. Hyatt is one of the top transfer partners for Chase, and I’ve had incredible luck staying at top properties using Hyatt points, such as all-inclusive Dreams hotels in Cancun, Mexico, and Punta Cana, Dominican Republic, the Hyatt Regency Koh Samui in Thailand, and the Hyatt Regency Kotor Bay in Montenegro — many of which I transferred from Chase. The water park and lazy river at the Dreams Onyx in Punta Cana. Image Credit: Lori Zaino For new cardholders of the Chase Sapphire Preferred card (existing cardholders can continue to transfer at the 1:1 ratio until October 1, 2026), the transfer ratio to Hyatt is now 4:3 , which means you’re technically losing 33% of your points on every Hyatt transfer . The Chase Sapphire Reserve card’s transfer ratio to Hyatt is a solid 1:1 . So while both cards offer largely the same redemption options, the Hyatt ratio is a dealbreaker at redemption time. It’s also worth noting that you can get more value ( up to 2.5 cents per point ) with Chase Points Boost using your Chase Sapphire Reserve card. Because of this, the Chase Sapphire Reserve card wins in the redemptions category . » Related: Should You Upgrade to the Chase Sapphire Reserve To Keep 1:1 Hyatt Transfers? Annual Fee The annual fees on these cards are wildly different — $700 different, to be exact. The Chase Sapphire Reserve card has an annual fee of $795, while the Chase Sapphire Preferred card has a much more affordable annual fee of $95. The Chase Sapphire Preferred card is the obvious winner in this category, thanks to its lower fee . But as I mentioned above, both cards’ value is tied to the ability to offset the annual fee by using their benefits. So, while the Chase Sapphire Preferred card does have a lower fee, if the benefits of the Chase Sapphire Reserve card resonate with you and you’ll be able to use them, this card could be the winner in your case. Final Thoughts Deciding whether the Chase Sapphire Reserve card or the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is right for you depends mostly on your spending, travel, and lifestyle habits — and what you’re willing to pay in annual fees. If you frequently spend on airlines and hotels, have the ability to use and stay on top of many statement credits, value airport lounge access, want the most premium Chase card available, and don’t mind paying a high fee, the Chase Sapphire Reserve card should be your pick. If you’d rather pay a lower annual fee, spend a lot on gas, dining, travel, and streaming, and don’t use Hyatt as a transfer partner, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is probably right for you. And if you’re truly dedicated to earning Chase Ultimate Rewards points, get both cards and be savvy about what spending you put on each in order to best maximize each card’s bonus categories and benefits.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/investing_news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"All News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Boeing beats Airbus with 173 plane orders at Farnborough Airshow\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/boeing-beats-airbus-with-173-plane-orders-at-farnborough-airshow-4809116\",\"image\":\"https://i-invdn-com.investing.com/news/LYNXMPED3P0U2_M.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:29:37.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/diem-bao.33/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Điểm báo\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Forum\",\"title\":\"\\\"Vì việc làng, đất vàng cũng hiến”\",\"link\":\"https://voz.vn/t/vi-viec-lang-dat-vang-cung-hien%E2%80%9D.1263286/unread\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvoz.vn%2Ft%2Fvi-viec-lang-dat-vang-cung-hien%25E2%2580%259D.1263286&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dvoz.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:29:03.000Z\",\"createDate\":\"2026-07-23T20:15:18+0700\",\"content\":\"Hàng chục hộ dân đã tự nguyện dỡ rào, hiến đất, nhường đi những tấc đất quý giá để những cung đường mới khang trang, rộng mở - PV Báo Công an nhân dân vừa ghi nhận được câu chuyện đầy ý nghĩa này ở xã miền núi Hiệp Đức, TP Đà Nẵng. Lan tỏa rộng khắp tinh thần “vì việc làng, đất vàng cũng hiến” Thời gian qua, kể từ khi triển khai thực hiện c