avicons?domain=kenh14.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Entertainment\",\"title\":\"150 nghìn đồng có đủ chơi trọn Sun World Sam Son?\",\"link\":\"https://kenh14.vn/150-nghin-dong-co-du-choi-tron-sun-world-sam-son-215260723192409708.chn\",\"image\":\"https://kenh14cdn.com/zoom/600_315/203336854389633024/2026/7/23/photo1784803603408-1784803603693592603144-1784809451206424484711.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Chỉ với 150.000 đồng/người, du khách có thể khám phá trọn vẹn công viên nước lớn bậc nhất miền Bắc với tổ hợp trò chơi dành cho mọi lứa tuổi. Chương trình vé đồng giá được Sun World Sam Son áp dụng cho tất cả các ngày trong tuần từ 27/7.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://genk.vn/rss/home.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Genk.vn\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=genk.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Áp lực sống hiện đại quá tải: Các nhà khoa học cảnh báo bộ não con người đang bị đẩy tới hạn mức chịu đựng\",\"link\":\"https://genk.vn/ap-luc-song-hien-dai-qua-tai-cac-nha-khoa-hoc-canh-bao-bo-nao-con-nguoi-dang-bi-day-toi-han-muc-chiu-dung-165260723111427051.chn\",\"image\":\"https://genk.mediacdn.vn/zoom/700_438/139269124445442048/2026/7/23/avatar1784779994997-17847799953281257749501.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Nghiên cứu mới từ các nhà khoa học Singapore cho thấy sự phát triển vượt bậc của xã hội hiện đại đang tạo ra \\\"sự lệch pha tiến hóa\\\", khiến trí óc và cơ thể con người phải gồng gánh những áp lực vượt quá khả năng sinh học tự nhiên.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Top 5 Reasons To Choose Royalton Vessence Barbados for an All-Inclusive Marriott Stay [Review]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/travel/hotels/royalton-vessence-barbados-review/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Royalton-Vessence-Barbados-view-from-beach-wide.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-23T13:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The author was a guest of Royalton Vessence Barbados Adult-Oriented, an Autograph Collection All-Inclusive Resort .  All opinions are the author’s own, and Royalton Vessence Barbados had no input in any part of this review. I watched a sea turtle surface for a breath, as if flying from the crystal-clear depths of the ocean, only to plunge just as suddenly back to the sandy floor. A stingray then glided past, and I looked through my snorkel mask at my husband with more than an expression of disbelief. Just a few strokes away was our resort, the newly opened Royalton Vessence Barbados . This property marks the debut of the Royalton Vessence brand, which says it promotes the “art of vacation.” This concept extended to multiple aspects of our 4-night stay in July 2026, including curated spaces, globally inspired dining, and a suite of activities. Here’s what made Royalton Vessence Barbados stand out and why you should consider it for a stay. 1. You Can Earn or Burn Marriott Bonvoy Points Cash rates at Royalton Vessence Barbados Adult-Oriented, an Autograph Collection All-Inclusive Resort , for the most affordable suite start at $657 in summer and rise to over $1,400 over the peak winter season. Award nights start at 95,500 Marriott Bonvoy points in low season and climb as high as 169,000 points in peak season (offering 0.6 to 0.8 cents per point in value, which is about where we value Marriott Bonvoy points ). Because of the higher award night cost, this property would be a good candidate for a topped-up Free Night Award , or more ideally, you could take advantage of Marriott’s fifth-night-free benefit to get 5 award nights for the price of 4. Hot Tip: The welcome offer from the Marriott Bonvoy Brilliant® American Express® Card can help boost your points balance. It also comes with an annual Free Night Award of up to 85,000 points and automatic Marriott Bonvoy Platinum Elite status . Our guide to the best Marriott Bonvoy credit cards compares the benefits and perks of each available card. 2. Upgrade to Diamond Club for a Premium Experience Diamond Club guests in any room category can enjoy: Check in and out at the Diamond Club Lounge , with access all day to premium food and drinks Butler service , which includes instant messaging access, assistance with unpacking, and help with dining reservations Preferential room locations Priority beach and pool areas Welcome amenities An upgraded minibar 1-hour hydrotherapy access Diamond Club is complimentary for Marriott Bonvoy Platinum Elite, Titanium Elite, and Ambassador Elite members, plus 1 guest. But if you don’t have status, is it worth springing for? When guests book via Marriott.com , the Diamond Club upcharge adds about $200 to $250 per night to the only non-Diamond Club room available, a junior suite with a garden view. Diamond Club wristband. Our butlers,  Kaleifa and Taneah,  messaged me daily wit h activity times, the dining venues and their opening times, and any booking confirmations. They quickly addressed my various requests. Bottom Line: If you prefer an ocean view or a swim-out suite, those rooms are only bookable as Diamond Club. If you’re considering a garden-view room but having access to a butler, top-tier beverages, and prime positioning at the pool or beach is a priority, spring for the Diamond Club. 3. Enjoy Curated Spaces Made for Relaxation and Rest The design of our swim-out junior suite was inviting. Its wood features paired well with vibrant, heavy accent rugs , and pops of patterns and notes of blue, green, and orange gave the room a contemporary feel . In the main room, a firm chaise lounge with a coffee table was across from the desk and minibar area. Opposite the king-size bed was a large flat-screen TV above a drawer unit with shelving. The bed was firm and delivered a relaxing night’s rest. Each side had a nightstand, an eyemask, light switches, a universal power outlet, and USB-A and USB-C inputs. Swim-Out Pool The suites featuring swim-out pools are among the highest-category rooms, commanding rates higher than those of 1-bedroom or ocean-view suites (ours was around $1,800 per night for our stay). The majority of these suites face a greenery buffer near the lobby, though some are closer to the main pool and beach. Our patio featured comfortable lounge chairs and in-pool loungers with a privacy screen to block the view of the adjoining suite. All-Inclusive Room Perks Several enhancements made this room stand out, starting with a complimentary beach bag hand-painted by a local artist. Upon arrival, we received fruit and bottles of wine and rum. The next day, full-size liquor bottles appeared. The minibar had juices, water bottles, Coke products, and Banks and Deputy beers. Standard coffee and tea service was also available. Bathroom As we stepped into the room, a small toilet room with a sliding door was immediately on the left, ahead of an open space with a double vanity and a massive shower, all tiled in white and gray marble. The Vessence-branded bath amenities had a refreshing green tea scent. Across from the vanity was a closet with robes, slippers, yoga mats, and an umbrella. 4. Discover Globally Inspired Flavors All meals and beverages at the 13 restaurants and 3 bars were included in the all-inclusive experience. Primary dining: Barista: all-day coffee shop Evo: all-day lobby bar Essenza: breakfast buffet Hunter Steakhouse: dinner-only La Scala: dinner-only Italian cuisine La Scala To Go: lunch-only pizza window Kai: dinner-only Asian cuisine Moi Aussi: dinner-only French cuisine Nabū: daytime swim-up bar Petisco: lunch-only bar and grill Room 21: dinner and late-night sports bar The Rooftop lunch-only outposts: Catrinas Express: Mexican cuisine Little Waves: seafood Rooftop Bar The Saffron Hut: Indian cuisine Sugar Halo: pastries and sweets During my visit, breakfast was at Essenza, lunch was limited to Petisco and The Rooftop, and dinner rotated (Hunter and La Scala alternated days open with Moi Aussi and Kai, with Room 21 open nightly). Room service was also available. Hot Tip: The Royalton Luxury All-Inclusive Resorts app features menus and hours for each dining location. Breakfast at Essenza Essenza has floor-to-ceiling views, and relaxing with a drink and watching the catamarans breeze by was a highlight of every morning. Breakfast with a view. The buffet area was spacious, with just about everything you’d expect. Buffet area. Chilled stations featured yogurt, fruit, charcuterie, and salad, while hot stations offered fritters, fried plantains, breakfast meats, pizza, and pancakes. Guests could order custom eggs and request carved meat. Lunch We enjoyed lunch at open-air Petisco, with starters like conch fritters and chicken wings and mains such as flank steak and cheeseburgers. One afternoon, we also ordered a pizza from the abbreviated La Scala menu. The Rooftop concept offers 4 quick-service lunch venues and a bar. This area felt like it was finding its footing, with limited food availability and staffing. My favorite was the Indian outpost, The Saffron Hut . My husband and I shared lamb rogan josh and chicken tikka, and both were stellar. Lunch at The Saffron Hut. Dinner With 4 nights, we were able to dine at each of the primary dinner restaurants. The ribeye at Hunter was a highlight of our first night, with the lamb chops from La Scala a spectacular standout. We went all out at Moi Aussi, ordering duck confit, beef bourguignon, and tenderloin , and all were excellent. Our least favorite meal was at Kai , the Asian restaurant. The sushi, tom yum soup, and red curry missed the mark, but the braised pork belly redeemed the meal. We visited during the World Cup and popped into Room 21 to catch a game, but the bright lighting and seating didn’t deliver a sports-bar atmosphere. Bottom Line: The dinner restaurants were brightly lit and could get quite noisy with just a few tables. More private, intimate dining spaces would be welcome. Bars and Anytime Eats We enjoyed bantering with the friendly staff at Nabū and Barista, who were more than happy to offer recommendations for their favorite concoctions or ice cream flavors. 5. Connect With Outdoor, Wellness, and Creative Activities The app listed daily fitness classes, pool activities, creative classes at The Studio, and nightly entertainment. Nothing overlapped, and it was easy to put together a rough schedule for the day (or zero schedule at all). Pools Main Pool The expansive pool was surrounded by a variety of loungers. Diamond Club guests had access to preferential padded loungers, and butlers could arrange a towel on a poolside chair ahead of a guest’s visit. We enjoyed the sunset each night from the massive hot tub, which was one of the largest I’ve seen. Diamond Club Rooftop Pool Diamond Club guests have access to an infinity-edge pool and hot tub on The Rooftop, open until 2 a.m. Holetown Beach The hotel had several rows of umbrellas and loungers — some padded for Diamond Club and others unpadded. The public beach itself was not very long, but the section at the Royalton was wide and free of sargassum. The boardwalk extended, with a mix of concrete paths and beach access, for a nice walk in either direction. Holetown boardwalk. Cabanas and Beds Bali beds dotted the beach and pool area, with larger cabanas featuring sofas and tables poolside. At the time of my visit, all of these were available without reservation or upcharge. Water Sports Nonmotorized water sports were part of the all-inclusive package, including kayaks, stand-up paddleboards, an Aqua Cycle, a Hobie Cat, and snorkel equipment. We were enamored by the fantastic snorkeling. Shallow artificial rock reefs were just a few steps from the beach and teeming with sea life. We saw angelfish, parrotfish, blue tangs, pufferfish, and seemingly endless more varieties. We snorkeled at various times of day and at different tides, and it was consistently excellent. Artificial reefs as seen from the hotel. Hot Tip: The area where the catamaran tours stop offshore is where you can snorkel to see turtles, stingrays, and tarpon. Grab a neon snorkel marker from the water sports desk to make yourself more visible to boats. The Royal Spa As Diamond Club guests, my husband and I enjoyed an hour at the hydrotherapy pool and hot tub in the spa. The sauna and steam rooms were gender-specific by locker room, and there were 3 types of showers in the hydrotherapy area. Spa services include facials, massages, and body treatments. Moddo Fitness by Royalton FIT The fitness center had everything needed to work out away from home, with cardio and strength-training equipment from Technogym. Activities at The Studio Our kids were at camp the week we spent in Barbados, and I felt like we had an adult camp experience ourselves. My husband stepped completely out of his comfort zone and joined me at The Studio for a painting class, a tie-dye experience, and a pottery session. Hot Tip: The resort is adult-oriented but not adults-only. We did see small children during our stay, but there is no family or kid-specific programming. Nightly Entertainment Musicians performed in the lobby after sunset. The sounds were inescapable in our room, but everything was quiet by 10 p.m. Dancers and musicians. Final Thoughts Royalton Vessence Barbados is ready to welcome guests, who will find friendly staff, relaxing spaces, a varied dining program, and a solid schedule of activities. If all we did on a return visit was snorkel and retreat to the hot tub with a Banks in hand, I think my husband would call that a successful vacation.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://kenh14.vn/home.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Kenh14\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.co