át triển ngành công nghiệp bán dẫn, câu chuyện của Đài Loan mang lại nhiều gợi ý quan... Click to expand... Read more\",\"replyCount\":269,\"viewCount\":33000},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/chuyen-tro-linh-tinh-tm.17/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Chuyện trò linh tinh™\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Forum\",\"title\":\"Khám sức khỏe xin việc tốn hết 450k quá sốc\",\"link\":\"https://voz.vn/t/kham-suc-khoe-xin-viec-ton-het-450k-qua-soc.1262985/unread\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvoz.vn%2Ft%2Fkham-suc-khoe-xin-viec-ton-het-450k-qua-soc.1262985&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dvoz.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:32:51.000Z\",\"createDate\":\"2026-07-23T02:32:51+0700\",\"content\":\"Nay có quy định mới hay gì hả các bác, chiều qua đi 2 bệnh viện đa khoa đều y chang nhau, nói rõ với nó là \\\"khám sức khỏe để xin việc\\\" thì nó kêu nay quy định mới phải khám theo thông tư mới gì đó, có cả chụp x-quang, xét nghiệm máu. Mấy năm trước mình khám tầm hơn 100k chứ nhiêu, quái lạ nay sao nó đẻ ra lắm vậy, chỉ là khám sức khỏe để làm hồ sơ đi xin việc thôi mà Đi phòng khám tư thấy báo giá 450k tưởng bịp nên chạy qua phòng khám công (huyện) cũng y vậy nên ngậm ngùi khám luôn\",\"replyCount\":58,\"viewCount\":3000},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://baomoi.com/\",\"feedTitle\":\"Nhân Dân điện tử • Kinh tế,Video,Media Kinh tế\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=nhandan.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"News\",\"title\":\"[Video] Phạt đến 100 triệu đồng nếu che giấu thông tin về thuế\",\"link\":\"https://nhandan.vn/video-phat-den-100-trieu-dong-neu-che-giau-thong-tin-ve-thue-post977237.html\",\"image\":\"https://photo-baomoi.bmcdn.me/w250_r3x2/2026_07_23_14_55673480/73785a14145ffd01a44e.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:32:09.494Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"[Video] Phạt đến 100 triệu đồng nếu che giấu thông tin về thuế\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Buy Choice Privileges Points With a 40% Discount [Until August 28]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/choice-privileges-buy-points/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Comfort-Hotel-Grand-Central-exterior.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:25:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Choice Privileges members have a new offer to buy Choice points with a 40% discount. If maximized, this sale matches the best price we’ve ever seen for buying Choice points. This offer is available through August 28, 2026. Choice may not be the first hotel chain that comes to mind for many travelers, but with this discount, you could unlock some great redemptions around the world. Here’s a look at everything you should know. Buy Choice Privileges Points — The Details Choice Privileges frequently offers a discount or bonus on purchased points, though the amount varies. The current offer features a  40% discount for targeted members, a vailable for a limited time . If maximized, this promotion will reduce the cost of buying points to 0.62 cents each . This offer has a single tier, though not all members are seeing the same offer. If you have the 40% discount offer, here are the details: Buy 1,000 to 5,000 points without a discount Buy 6,000+ points with a 40% discount (0.62 cents each) Direct link to offer Image Credit: Choice Your specific discount may vary, as this is a targeted offer from Choice Privileges . This promotion is valid through  August 28, 2026, and you can buy up to 180,000 points before the bonus. Hot Tip: Choice Privileges points are sold through Points.com , so they won’t code as a travel or hotel purchase. To get the best return when purchasing Choice Privileges points, use an everyday spending card like the Capital One Venture X Rewards Credit Card or the Capital One Venture Rewards Credit Card to earn 2x miles per $1 spent, or the  Chase Freedom Unlimited® to earn 1.5% cash-back .  Is It Worth It? Although there isn’t much buzz around Choice Privileges points, there are numerous instances when buying them can make sense. Choice Hotels has thousands of properties worldwide , and while many of these aren’t ultra-high-end, you can score some good value. Amerikalinjen, Ascend Hotel Collection, in Oslo, Norway. Image Credit: Keri Stooksbury There are a few things to know about Choice points in general: Choice doesn’t charge more for additional guests (up to the capacity limit). Suites cost the same as standard rooms in points. At Upgraded Points, we value Choice Privileges points at 0.6 cents apiece. Thus, this 40% discount means you’re still buying points at a price slightly above their typical value . Moreover, it’s certainly possible to get more than 0.62 cents per point in value, depending on how you redeem Choice Privileges points . If you can redeem at a good value, buying during this offer can be a great way to save money — especially if you were going to pay cash for a hotel and the cost of buying the needed points is cheaper. » Related: July 2026 Buy Points Promotions and Bonuses Other Ways To Earn Choice Privileges Points In addition to purchasing Choice points, you can also  earn Choice Privileges points in several other ways . Wells Fargo Rewards points transfer to Choice Privileges at a 1:2 ratio , while Citi ThankYou Rewards Points transfer at a 1:1.5 rate. You can also transfer your Amex Membership Rewards points and Capital One miles to Choice at a 1:1 ratio; however, these options aren’t ideal. Citi and Wells Fargo offer better transfer rates. You can also earn Choice points from everyday spending and welcome offers on 2 credit cards issued by Wells Fargo in the U.S.: the Choice Privileges® Mastercard® and Choice Privileges® Select Mastercard® . Final Thoughts As with previous offers, this is a targeted promotion, offering a 40% discount when you buy Choice Privileges points. If you have this offer, you can purchase Choice points at a reasonable price by buying at least 6,000 points in a single transaction. Choice offers numerous discounts and bonuses when purchasing points throughout the year, and this is among the better offers we’ve seen. If you want to take advantage, purchase before the sale ends on August 28, 2026.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=100003114\",\"feedTitle\":\"US Top News and Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"‘Out-of-favor’ utilities could be the next beneficiaries of the AI trade – and they pay dividends, Wells Fargo says\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/22/utilities-that-could-be-the-next-beneficiaries-of-ai-trade.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F22%2Futilities-that-could-be-the-next-beneficiaries-of-ai-trade.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:23:30.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"A few overlooked names in the utilities sector could be poised for gains, the bank said.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Hacker News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=news.ycombinator.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"John C. Dvorak has died\",\"link\":\"https://twitter.com/na_announce/status/2079952538040672302\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ftwitter.com%2Fna_announce%2Fstatus%2F2079952538040672302&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dnews.ycombinator.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:22:19.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Comments\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Argentina Economy Shrinks Again in May Amid Uneven Recovery\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-22/argentina-economy-shrinks-for-second-month-amid-uneven-recovery\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-22%2Fargentina-economy-shrinks-for-second-month-amid-uneven-recovery&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:15:22.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Argentina’s economy contracted for a second straight month in May, underscoring a trend of uneven growth more than halfway through President Javier Milei’s term.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Price-hiked iPads are a little cheaper right now\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/969003/apple-ipad-air-pro-airtag-deal-sale\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/apple-ipad-pro-m5-roundup-deal.png?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:14:31.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The iPad Pro M5 is one of the iPads discounted for the sale. | Image: The Verge A number of Apple products got more expensive last month, so we’re happy to find deals wherever and whenever we can. If you’re searching for a high-end iPad, one of the more notable deals currently happening is on the 13-inch iPad Pro M5 with 512GB of storage. Normally $1,699, it’s $150 off at Amazon , costing $1,549.99. It’s $100 off at Best Buy . This is the most premium iPad that Apple sells, with impressive performance from its M5 processor, a gorgeous OLED screen, up to 60W of fast charging, and support for the Apple Pencil Pro and Magic Keyboard. Read our iPad Pro (2025) review . 13-inch iPad Pro (2025) Where to Buy: $1699 $1599 at Best Buy (512GB, Wi-Fi) $1699 $1549 at Amazon (512GB, Wi-Fi) There’s also a deep discount on some configurations of the 11-inch iPad Air M3 . This model sports 1TB of storage, an optional 5G cellular connection, and it’s marked down to $749, a $500 discount from the suggested retail price. While the M3 chip is on the older side, you get 1TB of storage for just $40 more than the base M4 version with 128GB . The discount is available in all four colors: blue , purple , space gray , and starlight . Read our Apple iPad Air M3 review . 11-inch iPad Air M3 The last-gen 11-inch iPad Air comes with Apple’s M3 chip and GPU upgrades. It’s available in dark gray, blue, purple, and a “starlight” cream shade. Read our review . Where to Buy: $1249 $749 at Best Buy (1TB, Wi-Fi + 5G) Other deals to consider Sony is selling refurbished Playstation 5 Slim consoles for $499, a $100 break from the usual price. They may have some minor cosmetic imperfections, but are tested and certified by Sony to perform just as well as a new console. These slightly older digital only models have the full 1TB of storage, as opposed to the newer 825GB models, and have a one year warranty in case there are any issues. Normally $99.99, a four pack of the second-generation Apple AirTags are on sale for $89.99 at Amazon , matching their lowest price ever. The updated version of Apple’s popular Bluetooth tracker boosts the speaker volume, making it easier to find your stuff, and have more precise tracking. They’re still easy to setup, with one-touch pairing on iOS devices, and will run for over a year on a single replaceable battery. Amazon has the Razer Viper V3 Pro wireless gaming mouse listed for $99.99, about $30 lower than its usual price. The symmetrical mouse features an 8K polling rate and 35K DPI sensor, specs that will let you customize it to your play style, and eight programmable buttons to put every action right where you need it. At just 54 grams, the Viper V3 Pro is impressively lightweight, yet it still manages to last 95 hours of battery life on a single charge. There are plenty of less expensive gaming mice on the market, but this one’s well-rounded.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"iOS code could reportedly let Apple cut off apps when users miss iPhone payments\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/969596/apple-restricted-mode-ios-27\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/06/DSC03775_processed.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T19:13:21.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Code found in an iOS 27 beta would allow Apple to put a financed iPhone in \\\"Restricted Mode\\\" if it detects any missed payments, 9to5Mac reports . The finding follows a story from Bloomberg earlier this week claiming Apple is preparing to launch a new \\\"Apple Upgrade\\\" financing program for leasing new devices. iPhones in \\\"Restricted Mode\\\" would reportedly lose access to nearly all apps, except for basics like the Phone app, Settings, and the App Store. It uses a new \\\"App Managed Features\\\" system that allows financing or partner apps to continually check if a financed device is in good standing. According to 9to5Mac , the code also includes a … Read the full story at The Verge.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/diem-bao.33/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Điểm báo\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedC