:\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/award-alert-us-seoul-business-class/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Bongeunsa-Temple-exterior-Seoul.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T16:40:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Raise your hand if you want a great deal on lie-flat seats over the Pacific so you can arrive in South Korea rested and ready to explore all the country has to offer. If you’re looking for an incredible trip next year without breaking the bank, take a look at this deal, which can get you to Seoul in comfort and style. Even better, there are up to 9 seats available in business class on some dates. You’ll be flying Asiana Airlines with a lie-flat seat, arriving in Korea rested and ready to explore. Here’s how to book it for yourself. Award Deal to Seoul — The Details We’re seeing wide-open award availability for Asiana Airlines business class between the West Coast and Seoul (ICN), with seats priced at 85,000 Air Canada Aeroplan points each way on dates in July and August 2026. If you’ve been looking for a comfortable way to fly to South Korea this summer, this is a great opportunity to do so. Class:  Business Program: Air Canada Aeroplan Route: Los Angeles (LAX), Seattle (SEA), and San Francisco (SFO) to Seoul (ICN) Cost: 85,000 points plus $56 in taxes Travel dates:  July and August 2026 Award seats:  Up to 9 passengers per route in business The best availability is for July, but there are also dates scattered throughout August as well. You’ll book flights through Aeroplan, paying 85,000 points per person. You can use a tool like Seats.aero to get an overview of multiple dates and routes at once. Image Credit: Seats.aero Paying 85,000 points per person on this route is a good price for business class, no matter how you slice it — especially since finding saver-level awards to South Korea is uncommon. Even better, taxes and fees are minimal on these flights at CAD$78.80 (roughly $56). » Related: The Best Ways To Fly to South Korea With Points and Miles [Step by Step] How To Book After finding seats through a tool like Seats.aero , book these award flights using Aeroplan points : Image Credit: Air Canada Luckily, earning Aeroplan points is very easy. You can spend on Air Canada’s Aeroplan credit card or transfer points from Amex Membership Rewards , Bilt Rewards , Capital One miles , Chase Ultimate Rewards , Marriott Bonvoy , and Rove Miles . Final Thoughts If you’re planning a trip to Asia this summer, this award alert could be one of the best ways to use your points —- especially if you’re hoping to travel in comfort. For those saving points for a special trip or a family getaway, this is the kind of opportunity that’s worth jumping on. Be sure to act fast and secure your seats before availability disappears.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSMarketsMain\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: Markets\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Health Care Roundup: Market Talk\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/articles/health-care-roundup-market-talk-bbde9678?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-26903776\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T16:36:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"george frey/Reuters\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Apple is reportedly testing a MacBook Neo with more RAM\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/969434/apple-macbook-neo-a19-pro-ram-upgrade\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/04/268442_Apple_MacBook_Neo_competition_Lenovo_Acer_Asus_ADiBenedetto_0002.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-22T16:35:58.000Z\",\"createDate\":