points.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Preferred Hotels Last-Minute Escapes: Save up to 35% [Book by August 3]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/preferred-hotels-last-minute-escapes/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Half-Moon-Bay-Jamaica-Preferred-Hotels.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:28:30.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Preferred Hotels is offering savings of up to 35% if you book your trip soon — by August 3, to be clear. This is part of the chain’s recurring Last Minute Escapes promotion, and the latest round of this offer applies to stays through September 3, 2026. There are 66 hotels eligible this time around. If you have travel plans in the near future, there are big savings available at Preferred Hotels properties in numerous countries. Here’s a closer look at the details. Preferred Hotels Cyber Sale Details Preferred Hotels is a brand that doesn’t get as much attention as mega brands like Hyatt, Hilton, or IHG, but it shouldn’t be ignored. With over 650 independent hotels and resorts across 85 countries, it offers some unique options for travelers. If you’re planning hotel stays between now and September 3, 2026, check out Preferred Hotels’ Last Minute Escapes promotion. With this offer , you can save up to 35% at 75 participating locations worldwide, and you don’t need a promo code to get these savings. This sale is available for travel booked by August 3, 2026 . While the sale itself doesn’t have any minimum stay requirements, individual properties might impose blackout dates or obligate you to stay a minimum number of nights. There are 75 hotels bookable through the Last Minute Escapes promotion, including: Mayfair House Hotel & Garden in Miami Haven Riviera Cancun NANNAI Muro Alto in Brazil Hotel New Otani Tokyo Save up to 35% at the Mayfair House Hotel & Garden in Miami. Image Credit: Mayfair House Hotel & Garden You must be a Preferred Hotels I Prefer member to be eligible for these savings and to earn points from your upcoming hotel stays. If you aren’t already a member, you can join I Prefer here . Joining is free, and this lets you start participating in the I Prefer program right away. Bottom Line: Save up to 35% on select Preferred Hotels locations when you book by August 3 and stay by September 3, 2026. There aren’t any promo codes or minimum stay requirements for this offer, but only select properties are eligible. Final Thoughts Select Preferred Hotels locations are on sale for travel through September 3, 2026. Members who book by August 3 can save up to 35% on their hotel reservations at 75 different properties across the world. This presents considerable savings for those needing a hotel stay soon — hence the name of the Last Minute Escapes promotion.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=100003114\",\"feedTitle\":\"US Top News and Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"How to use options to play 'a sizable reversion move' in Micron over the next few days\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/21/how-to-use-options-to-play-a-sizable-reversion-move-in-micron-over-the-next-few-days.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F21%2Fhow-to-use-options-to-play-a-sizable-reversion-move-in-micron-over-the-next-few-days.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:26:51.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The memory chip maker rocketed nearly 70% in five weeks, peaking above $1,250 in late June, only to surrender 35% of that value in the 22 days since.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://baomoi.com/\",\"feedTitle\":\"Tiền Phong • Kinh tế,Doanh nghiệp\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=tienphong.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"News\",\"title\":\"PNJ xin lỗi trước làn sóng 'bán tháo' kim cương\",\"link\":\"https://tienphong.vn/pnj-xin-loi-truoc-lan-song-ban-thao-kim-cuong-post1861522.tpo\",\"image\":\"https://photo-baomoi.bmcdn.me/w500_r3x2/2026_07_21_20_55665123/01aad36b9d20747e2d31.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:26:26.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"PNJ xin lỗi trước làn sóng 'bán tháo' kim cương\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/chuyen-tro-linh-tinh-tm.17/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Chuyện trò linh tinh™\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Forum\",\"title\":\"Các bác đi làm Nhà nước giờ thế nào?\",\"link\":\"https://voz.vn/t/cac-bac-di-lam-nha-nuoc-gio-the-nao.1220351/unread\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvoz.vn%2Ft%2Fcac-bac-di-lam-nha-nuoc-gio-the-nao.1220351&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dvoz.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:26:14.000Z\",\"createDate\":\"2026-03-22T10:26:03+0700\",\"content\":\"Phường, xã giờ đi làm căng thẳng, áp lực quá các bác à, giờ việc nó nặng lên gấp 7, 8 lần, như chỗ em thì nặng lên cả hàng chục lần Phường, xã giờ gánh hết cả 2 cấp, gánh cả cấp quận, huyện và các phường, xã trước sáp nhập, lại còn thiếu người làm nữa, 1 người giờ thành làm việc của mấy người nhưng lương thì lại bị giảm Như em đi làm toàn tối đêm mới về, thứ 7, chủ nhật cũng không được nghỉ, lãnh đạo thì toàn ép việc vào ngày nghỉ, ngày lễ Lương thì bị mất 30% phụ cấp công tác Đảng, thưởng... Read more\",\"replyCount\":987,\"viewCount\":118000},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/chuyen-tro-linh-tinh-tm.17/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Chuyện trò linh tinh™\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Forum\",\"title\":\"Đã bao lâu messenger các bác chưa có một ai nhắn tin\",\"link\":\"https://voz.vn/t/da-bao-lau-messenger-cac-bac-chua-co-mot-ai-nhan-tin.1262605/unread\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvoz.vn%2Ft%2Fda-bao-lau-messenger-cac-bac-chua-co-mot-ai-nhan-tin.1262605&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dvoz.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:25:39.000Z\",\"createDate\":\"2026-07-21T21:24:47+0700\",\"content\":\"Hôm nay thử vào messenger mới nhận ra đã gần hai tháng chưa có ai nhắn tin, vừa năm trước còn học đại học bao nhiêu bạn bè rủ đi chơi rồi bàn chuyện rôm rả, giờ đi làm toàn tin nhắn zalo công việc, đồng nghiệp, nghĩ cũng chỉ thở nhẹ một cái ....\",\"replyCount\":64,\"viewCount\":3000},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Expedia’s One Key Rewards Changes Start Next Week: Tier-Based Earnings, Guarantees Gone, and No Flight Earnings\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/one-key-rewards-changes-2026/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Friends-on-ocean-wall-facing-away.jpeg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:22:30.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Expedia is overhauling how members earn OneKeyCash starting next week, on July 28, 2026. The changes introduce tier-based earning rates, eliminate rewards on flight bookings, and remove the Hotel Price Guarantee from both Expedia and Hotels.com (though the other changes below only apply to Expedia and not Hotels.com or Vrbo, which share the One Key program with Expedia). If you use One Key regularly, here’s what’s actually changing and who it affects. What’s Changing? Let’s look at each change in turn. There are a few of them. Earning Rates Are Now Tier-Based Previously, all One Key members earned up to 2% in OneKeyCash on eligible nonflight bookings regardless of status. Under the new structure, your earning rate will depend on your tier: Blue (0 to 4 trip elements): 1% Silver (5 to 14 trip elements): 2% Gold (15 to 29 trip elements): 2% Platinum (30 or more trip elements): 3% These new rates apply to Expedia only, which can feel confusing for a rewards program shared across 3 websites. Blue members take the biggest hit, with a 50% cut in base earning rate. If you’re a casual Expedia user without status, every dollar you spend on hotels and rentals now earns half of what it did before. Silver and Gold members come out roughly even. Platinum members actually see a modest improvement, going from 2% to 3%. One Key’s announcement of the changes (highlighting is ours). Image Credit: One Key VIP Access bonus earn rates are unchanged. Silver earns 3% total at VIP Access properties, Gold earns 4%, and Platinum earns 6%. Flights Earnings Are Gone The 0.2% earning rate on flights was already close to worthless. Now it’s gone entirely. After July 28, you won’t earn OneKeyCash on any flight bookings. The practical impact is minimal for most travelers; that 0.2% rate was rarely a reason to book through Expedia over booking directly with an airline or through a more rewarding portal. You can still enter your airline loyalty number at checkout to earn miles as usual. For packages that include flights — like a flight-plus-hotel bundle — you’ll earn at your tier rate on the nonflight elements only. Hotel Price Guarantee Is Gone Both Expedia and Hotels.com are eliminating the Hotel Price Guarantee , which previously compensated members who found a lower price after booking. There’s no replacement for it. What’s Coming Later in 2026? Gold and Platinum members will gain One Key Flight Delay Access sometime later this year , including lounge access or other experiences when an eligible flight is delayed by 90 minutes or more. No specific launch date has been announced beyond “later this year.” Your Existing Rewards Are Safe OneKeyCash already in your account keeps its value and expiration clock. Any trips booked before July 28, 2026, will earn at the rate in effect when you booked. Hot Tip: For those invested in the One Key program, holding either of the 2 One Key credit cards can make sense, based on extra earnings and extra perks they provide. Final Thoughts These changes are a clear win for Platinum members, a wash for Silver and Gold, and a loss for everyone at Blue status once they take effect on July 28. The loss of the Hotel Price Guarantee stings regardless of your membership tier. If you’re a Blue member using Expedia primarily for independent hotels or vacation rentals, the reduced earning rate is worth weighing against alternatives. Many hotel loyalty programs still offer more value than 1% back for members who book directly. The One Key program will likely still make sense the most for Vrbo bookings and for travelers without any brand loyalty, but the July 28 changes narrow its appeal at the entry level.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Russia Halts Bond Auctions With More Monetary Easing in Question\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-21/russia-halts-bond-auctions-with-more-monetary-easing-in-question\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-21%2Frussia-halts-bond-auctions-with-more-monetary-easing-in-question&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:20:56.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Russia halted auctions of domestic government bonds after a series of failed sales amid speculation the central bank may pause a year-long monetary easing cycle.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Singapore Airlines Now Requires Having KrisFlyer Miles in Your Account To Search Award Availability\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/singapore-airlines-krisflyer-award-search-miles-requirement/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Singapore-Airlines-A350-900.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T14:17:18.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"If you usually check Singapore Airlines award availability before deciding whether to transfer your credit card points, there’s a new catch. KrisFlyer members now need to have miles in their account before they can search for award flights online, making it much harder to search availability or plan future redemptions without an existing balance. Here’s what changed, why it matters, and what it could mean for anyone planning to book a Singapore Airlines award ticket. KrisFlyer Members Now Need Miles Before Searching Awards Without any advance warning, Singapore Airlines has introduced a new requirement for its KrisFlyer loyalty program . Members with a zero-mile balance can no longer search for award availability through the airline’s website or app. Instead, users are prompted to have a minimum balance in their KrisFlyer account before they can access award searches . While many reports suggest the threshold is 1,000 KrisFlyer miles , the message displayed on Singapore Airlines’ website doesn’t specify an exact amount. Instead, it simply states that the member’s current miles balance is insufficient to search for award flights . Message for users with 0 miles in their account. Image Credit: Singapore Airlines The airline has not officially announced the change, but frequent flyers have widely noticed it over the past day. Previously, anyone with a KrisFlyer account — even a brand-new account with no miles — could log in and search for award availability. That made it easy to check whether seats were available before deciding whether to transfer points from a credit card rewards program. The update is unlikely to affect existing KrisFlyer members who already keep miles in their accounts. However, it could create an extra step for new members or anyone whose balance is zero. Singapore Airlines hasn’t explained why it made the change, and it’s also unclear whether this is a permanent policy or something the airline is simply testing. For travelers, the biggest pain point is planning point transfers. KrisFlyer is a transfer partner of several major transferable points programs, such as American Express Membership Rewards , Capital One miles , Chase Ultimate Rewards , and Citi ThankYou Rewards (all at a ratio of 1:1), as well as Marriott Bonvoy at a transfer rate of 3:1 and Brex Rewards at a 3:2 ratio. Because transfers are generally one-way and can’t be reversed, many travelers like to confirm award availability before moving points into their KrisFlyer account. With this new change, someone opening a new KrisFlyer account may first need to transfer enough points to meet the required balance before they can even see if the flight they want is available. It’s a relatively small hurdle, but it’s an annoyance for travelers trying to plan an award booking. Hot Tip: Before transferring credit card points to any airline program , remember that most transfers are irreversible. Whenever possible, confirm award availability first to avoid getting stuck with miles you can’t immediately use. Final Thoughts Singapore Airlines hasn’t publicly commented on the change, so it’s unclear whether this is a permanent policy or simply something the airline is testing. We’re hoping it’s the latter. KrisFlyer has long been one of the best loyalty programs for accessing Singapore Airlines award space, and it’d be disappointing to see travelers face yet another hurdle before they can even start searching for flights.\",\