n the first 90 days of account opening . Samsung is launching its first credit card for U.S. consumers. Image Credit: Samsung The most compelling feature is arguably the 3% cash-back on purchases made through Samsung Wallet . If you already tap your Galaxy phone to pay for most of your everyday purchases, that bonus category could add up over time. Additionally, if you already subscribe to Samsung VIP Advantage — a paid membership that offers perks like discounts on Samsung products, extended return windows, and other exclusive benefits — you’ll also receive 20% off a membership purchase or renewal when paying with the Samsung Galaxy card. Beyond those benefits, however, the card has a niche appeal. Unless you’re already deep into Samsung’s ecosystem, this probably isn’t a card that will replace your everyday cash-back or travel rewards card . That said, if you’re interested in the Samsung Galaxy card, applications open on July 22, 2026, through Samsung’s U.S. website . Hot Tip: If you’re trying to decide whether the Samsung Galaxy card fits your wallet, check out our guide to the best no-annual-fee credit cards to see how it stacks up against other popular options. Final Thoughts If you already buy a lot of Samsung products and use Samsung Wallet for most of your everyday purchases, the Samsung Galaxy card could earn a place in your wallet. Otherwise, you’ll likely get more value from one of the best credit cards for everyday purchases , many of which offer stronger rewards across a wider range of spending categories.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/market_overview.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Market Overview\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"EUR/USD Under Pressure as Oil Prices Rise and ECB Meeting Looms\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/eurusd-under-pressure-as-oil-prices-rise-and-ecb-meeting-looms-200684247\",\"ima