le.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T17:57:59.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Hacker News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=news.ycombinator.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"That post never existed. Stop listening to that thing\",\"link\":\"https://rachelbythebay.com/w/2026/05/05/404/\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Frachelbythebay.com%2Fw%2F2026%2F05%2F05%2F404%2F&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dnews.ycombinator.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T17:57:37.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Comments\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Rakuten $50 Bonus Has Been Extended [$50 or 5,000 Amex Points]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/rakuten-new-member-50-bonus/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Person-using-computer-holding-credit-card.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T17:55:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Rakuten’s $50 referral bonus has been extended. Now, through September 30, 2026, you can earn $50 for each friend you refer, and your friend will earn $50 too . If you’re not a Rakuten member yet, you can use one of our referral links to earn your $50, and then you can refer your friends. Even better, you can opt to take your bonus as 5,000 Amex Membership Rewards points — and trust us, you’ll want to. We’ll show you why this choice can unlock far more value than expected. Here’s why you should be using Rakuten — and why right now is a great time to sign up. Get a $50 Bonus When You Join Rakuten Right now, Rakuten is offering $50 for new members, plus $50 to the person who refers them through September 30, 2026. For context, the typical bonus for new members is $30 or $40. Refer your friends, and you’ll each get $50. Image Credit: Rakuten To earn the bonus, you’ll need to make $50 worth of purchases within 90 days of joining Rakuten . If you do that, both you and the person who referred you will receive $50 — or 5,000 Amex Membership Rewards points. Because this deal requires a referral link, we’ve included some from our team to make it easy for you to access the offer: Andrew’s link Chris’ link Christine’s link Jarrod’s link Juan’s link Katie’s link Keri’s link Ryan’s link Hot Tip: You can also choose to earn Bilt Rewards through Rakuten, but unless you have Bilt elite status, the transfer ratio is just 1:0.5 ($10 cash-back equals 500 Bilt points). What Is Rakuten? Rakuten is an online shopping portal where you can find offers for bonus cash-back or points when shopping online. There’s also a convenient browser extension that you can install, and it will flash when you’re visiting a page with a current offer. Image Credit: Rakuten By clicking that button (or navigating through Rakuten’s website to the merchant you want to shop with) before finalizing your purchases, Rakuten will use trackers on your browser to verify the purchase. Then, you’ll receive a payout of the promised rewards. This can be a flat amount (for example, earning $20 after spending at least $200) or a certain rate (3% extra cash-back). The best value comes from the fact that Rakuten allows you to earn Amex Membership Rewards points, rather than cash-back , if you update the settings in your profile. We value Membership Rewards points at 2.2 cents each — more than double the value of earning cash-back rewards worth 1 cent apiece. Hot Tip: Choosing to earn Membership Rewards from online shopping is smart because the value you’ll get by transferring Amex points to hotel and airline partners will almost always be better than straight cash-back. Final Thoughts Now through September 30, 2026, you can earn a best-ever $50 bonus when you join Rakuten and spend at least $50 within 90 days. Even better, you can choose to take the bonus as 5,000 Amex Membership Rewards points — a far more valuable option.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"IHAK: There's No Future Without Cybersecurity And This ETF Reminds Us Of It\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4923521-ihak-theres-no-future-without-cybersecurity-and-this-etf-reminds-us-of-it?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4923521-ihak-theres-no-future-without-cybersecurity-and-this-etf-reminds-us-of-it%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T17:52:37.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"American Airlines Is Making Premium Travel at DFW Even Better — Here’s What To Expect\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/american-airlines-dfw-flagship-check-in-admirals-club/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/American-Airlines-B777-200ER-takeoff.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T17:51:19.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"If you regularly fly American Airlines through Dallas Fort Worth (DFW) in a premium cabin or with lounge access, your airport experience is about to get even better. The airline has announced several upgrades, from an exclusive check-in area to its largest Admirals Club ever. Here’s what you can expect. American Is Upgrading the Premium Experience at DFW American Airlines is investing in its biggest hub at Dallas Fort Worth International Airport (DFW) with several new features designed to make the airport experience smoother for premium travelers. Flagship Check-In Will Offer a More Private Airport Arrival The first addition arriving later this year is a dedicated Flagship check-in area in Terminal D , located near the D30 security checkpoint . Instead of checking in at the main ticket counters, eligible travelers will have access to a separate entrance with personalized assistance and a more private check-in process before heading directly to security. American’s new private Flagship check-in at DFW. Image Credit: American Airlines American hasn’t changed who can use the Flagship check-in. It’s generally available to customers flying in qualifying Flagship First or Flagship Business cabins , along with select AAdvantage elite members on eligible itineraries. The Largest Admirals Club Is Coming to DFW The airline is also building what will become the largest Admirals Club lounge in its network . The new lounge will span approximately 37,000 square feet inside Terminal C near the Skylink station , making it a convenient stop for travelers connecting through DFW. American says the space will include dedicated areas for working and relaxing, along with various seating options designed to accommodate different types of travelers. Food and beverage offerings are also getting an upgrade. Travelers can expect expanded all-day dining, chef-inspired menu items, an upgraded charcuterie selection, premium cocktails, wine, spirits, Champagne Bollinger, and Lavazza coffee — enhancements that have gradually rolled out across other Admirals Club locations. Hot Tip: The Citi®/AAdvantage® Executive World Elite Mastercard® includes Admirals Club membership, making it one of the easiest ways to enjoy American’s expanding lounge network, including the new DFW lounge when it opens. Terminal F Will Get a Grab-and-Go Admirals Club American is also thinking about travelers who don’t have time to sit down before boarding. As part of the future Terminal F expansion plans , the airline plans to open a Provisions by Admirals Club location. Rather than functioning as a traditional lounge, this concept is designed for travelers who simply want to grab fresh food, premium drinks, or travel essentials before heading to their gate. Provisions by Admiral will open at DFW in the near future for passengers wanting some snacks on the go. Image Credit: American Airlines While it’s not a full-service lounge, it should give eligible travelers a convenient place to pick up quality food and drinks before boarding. Hot Tip: American also recently announced it will open a new Provisions by Admirals Club at New York’s JFK airport . Final Thoughts While American hasn’t announced opening dates for the new lounges, the investments are part of a broader effort to modernize DFW as demand for premium travel continues to grow. Once they open, premium travelers can expect a smoother airport experience, whether that’s checking in faster, relaxing in a much larger lounge, or grabbing a bite before heading to the gate.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Judge pauses Paramount’s attempt to buy Warner Bros. Discovery\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/business/968055/paramount-wbd-merger-pause-tro\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/02/STKB385_PARAMOUNT_D.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T17:49:53.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"A judge partially granted the request from a dozen state 