Icon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"[Award Alert] Business Class to São Paulo, Brazil, for 50K Points in Business Class\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/award-alert-us-to-brazil-business-class/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Sao-Paulo-Brazil-parks-skyline.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T13:54:41.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"For anyone looking to fly to Brazil in comfort, we’ve found some great deals in business class with American Airlines to São Paulo (GRU). São Paulo is a mega city; it offers countless things to see and do. There are numerous tourist attractions and massive stadiums if you want to check out a Brazilian soccer match. There are museums galore, shopping, food, culture, and easy access to other cities in South America, given that this is the biggest city in the Americas. If you’re interested in visiting, you can arrive rested in a lie-flat business class seat for as few as 50,000 points one-way. Let’s check out the deal. Award Alert — Details Right now, you can find saver business class award availability flying with American Airlines , booked using Alaska Airlines Atmos Rewards points. We’re seeing multiple available dates from August 2026 to June 2027 , which isn’t common for business class to South America. If you’ve been thinking about booking a trip to Brazil, now is a great time to lock in the prices. Here are the details of what you can book: Class: Business Airline: American Airlines Award program: Alaska Airlines Atmos Rewards Route: Miami (MIA) and New York City (JFK) to São Paulo (GRU) Cost: From 50,000 points plus $18.10 one-way Travel dates: August 2026 to June 2027 Award seats: Up to 9 business class seats With many of these flights, you’ll fly in American Airlines business class on the Boeing 787-9 aircraft, offering a 1-2-1 layout. That means every passenger has direct aisle access. » Related: Is Brazil a Safe Place To Travel? A Personal Perspective How To Book While American Airlines lets you search with flexible dates, using a tool like Seats.aero is often one of the fastest ways to search for award tickets. You’ll find awards using Atmos Rewards points for 50,000 points per person, plus $18.10 in taxes and fees. 50k points to fly in business class to Brazil is a great deal. Image Credit: Seats.aero Once you’ve found a date that works, head to Alaska Airlines’ website to complete your booking. Image Credit: Alaska Airlines There are a few ways to earn Atmos Rewards points . You can use an Atmos Rewards credit card , shop through the Atmos Rewards Shopping portal , eat at restaurants that participate in Atmos Rewards Dining , fly with Oneworld partners, and more. Additionally, you can transfer from Bilt Rewards (1:1) and Marriott Bonvoy (3:1) to Atmos Rewards. Hot Tip: Want to travel to the Southern Hemisphere, but these dates don’t work for you? Check out our complete guide on the best ways to fly to South America using points and miles ! Final Thoughts Right now, you can book flights in business class from 2 different U.S. cities to São Paulo, Brazil, for just 50,000 points one-way. It’s rare to see award availability like this for cities deep in South America — especially for just 50k points. If you’ve been considering a trip, you’ll want to jump on this deal sooner rather than later to avoid missing out.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Electric air taxis go to war\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/transportation/967891/archer-evtol-military-anduril-air-taxi-thunder\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/Halo-Commercial-Variant-Full-Scale.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"