eateDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Emirates Unveils World-First Economy Headrest Designed To Help Passengers Sleep Better\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/emirates-economy-headrest/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Emirates-U-Dream-headrest-for-improved-sleep.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-20T13:03:53.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Your next flight with Emirates in economy could be comfier, thanks to this unique tweak. The Dubai-based airline is installing first-of-its-kind multiway adjustable headrests in some of its economy class cabins. “Emirates never rests on its laurels when it comes to customer experience, and we have found a way to significantly improve the comfort for Economy Class passengers, especially those traveling long-haul”, said Tim Clark, president of Emirates. Let’s take a look at this exciting update. Emirates U-Dream Headrest Debut on Airbus A350 Aircraft The world-first U-Dream headrests are already flying on three of Emirates ‘ Airbus A350s . According to the airline, passengers who’ve experienced the new headrests already are giving “outstanding praise”. The key feature of the game-changing side wings, which fold down around the passenger’s neck , and appear far more supportive than usual flappy headrest wings. The wings can also be folded inwards to help stop passengers’ heads tipping forward , jolting them awake. Emirates’ new U-Dream economy headrest. Image Credit: Emirates This innovative design provides more neck and head support than any other economy seat in the sky — so much so that it might even out-comfort many premium economy seats. Emirates is planning a fast installation, with the Safran economy seats on all of its Airbus A350s set to feature the U-Dream headrests by the end of the year. It won’t be until 2027 that the headrests will be added to the economy cabins of other aircraft types . To start with, only Emirates’ retrofitted Airbus A380 and Boeing 777s will have the headrests installed. All future deliveries of the long-awaited Boeing 777X will have the U-Dream headrests as standard. Who needs a travel neck pillow when you’ve got a U-Dream headrest? Image Credit: Emirates At the time of writing, Montréal (YUL) is the only airport in North America where Emirates flies its Airbus A350 . However, the aircraft operates on many of its Asian routes, so U.S.-based travelers could still experience the new product if connecting in Dubai (DXB). Hot Tip: Upgrade your comfort with more than just a fancy economy headrest and use points to fly Emirates business or even first class instead. Final Thoughts The U-Dream headrest certainly looks to be a winner. Being able to fall and stay asleep with proper head support is a dream come true for flyers who struggle to get proper rest in economy on long-haul flights. Emirates could have easily introduced this product only in a few front rows of economy and charged passengers for the privilege. Let’s hope this could be the start of a new age of economy class that takes the dread out of long overnight flights.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/commodities.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Commodities Analysis & Opinion\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Oil Import Costs Expose India’s Fiscal Vulnerability to Middle East Risk\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/oil-import-costs-expose-indias-fiscal-vulnerability-to-middle-east-risk-200684232\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Foil-import-costs-expose-indias-fiscal-vulnerability-to-middle-east-risk-200684232&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.goog