image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F19%2Fuks-incoming-pm-andy-burnham-to-prioritize-cost-of-living-say-allies.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-19T13:09:15.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The incoming prime minister plans to focus resources on pocketbook issues such as the cost of living, according to his allies.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/chuyen-tro-linh-tinh-tm.17/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Chuyện trò linh tinh™\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Forum\",\"title\":\"26 tuổi đi học lại ĐH\",\"link\":\"https://voz.vn/t/26-tuoi-di-hoc-lai-dh.1256474/unread\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvoz.vn%2Ft%2F26-tuoi-di-hoc-lai-dh.1256474&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dvoz.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-19T13:00:34.000Z\",\"createDate\":\"2026-07-01T13:51:37+0700\",\"content\":\"Nếu trong tay có khoảng số tiền cỡ 700tr và đi học lại bằng đại học mới, mất 2 năm thì cỡ 28-29 tuổi xong, thì có nên không nhỉ? Mình làm giáo viên tiếng Anh nhưng không đam mê với nghề, tính nhảy sang làm data/AI, nhưng để đi lâu dài với nghề thì cũng nên có tấm bằng đại học lận lưng. Nhiều lúc trăn trở là học xong ra làm fresher và bắt đầu lại từ đầu, và mấy em nhỏ hơn mình làm sếp của mình thì thấy cũng hơi tủi và nhiều khi còn bị khinh/bị chê nếu làm dở. Thấy mông lung với đời, nhưng... Read more\",\"replyCount\":117,\"viewCount\":14000},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Citi Double Cash Card vs. Wells Fargo Active Cash Card [Detailed Comparison]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/credit-cards/citi-double-cash-card-vs-wells-fargo-active-cash-card/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Citi-Double-Cash-Card-Wells-Fargo-Active-Cash-Card-Grocery-Upgraded-Points-LLC.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-19T13:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"There are several key reasons to choose a card that earns cash-back. Simplicity is near the top of the list, but earning well on nonbonus-category purchases and utilizing the associated card benefits are equally important. The Citi Double Cash® Card and Wells Fargo Active Cash® Card are 2 popular cards that consistently earn rewards on every purchase and offer some of the most liquid redemption options. In this article, we’ll compare these attributes and discuss the cards’ valuab le  introductory 0% APR benefits  that can help you save money on interest charges. Card Comparison Overview Before we discuss the details of the Double Cash card and the Wells Fargo Active Cash card , here is a quick overview for comparison purposes. SCROLL FOR MORE Feature or Benefit Citi Double Cash® Card Wells Fargo Active Cash® Card Welcome offer Earn $200 cash back after you spend $1,500 in the first 6 months of account opening. This bonus offer will be fulfilled as 20,000 ThankYou® Points, which can be redeemed for $200 cash back. Earn a $200 cash rewards bonus after spending $500 in purchases in the first 3 months. Top earning categories 5% cash-back on hotel, car rental, and attractions, excluding air travel, purchased through Citi Travel 2% cash-back on all other purchases (1% back when you buy and 1% back when you pay) Unlimited 2% cash rewards on every purchase Redemptions Redeem points for 1 cent each for travel through Citi Travel. Transfer points to airline and hotel partners. Credit to a Wells Fargo credit card, checking account, or mortgage. Access cash via Wells Fargo ATM. Top travel protections and benefits Mastercard Luxury Hotels and Resorts Lyft credit Automobile rental collision damage waiver Visa Signature Luxury Hotel Collection Top shopping protections and benefits Extended warranty Citi Merchant Offers Cell phone protection My Wells Fargo Deals Additional benefits 0% intro APR on balance transfers for 18 months. After that, the variable APR will be 17.49% to 27.49%. 0% intro APR for 12 months from account opening on purchases and qualifying balance transfers. 18.49%, 24.49% or 28.49% Variable APR thereafter Annual fees and authorized users $0 annual fee No additional fee to add authorized users $0 annual fee No additional fee to add authorized users Welcome Offer Comparison The Double Cash card and the Wells Fargo Active Cash card each come with a welcome offer that can be earned after meeting minimum spending requirements in the specified period following card approval. Here are the latest welcome offers and other important card information: Earning Potential The Double Cash card earns rewards in the form of Citi ThankYou Points that can be redeemed for cash-back, while the Wells Fargo Active Cash card earns cash-back rewards . We’ll discuss redemptions next, but first, let’s look at how you earn rewards on our featured cards: SCROLL FOR MORE Earning Category Double Cash Card Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Travel 5% cash-back on hotel, car rental, and attractions, excluding air travel, purchased through Citi Travel 2% cash-back All other purchases 2% cash-back (1% when making the purchase + 1% when paying the balance) 2% cash-back For those who pay their card balance in full each statement period, either card earns 2% cash-back. If you tend to carry a balance, you would earn more with the Wells Fargo Active Cash card . The difference is that the Double Cash card earns 1% on initial purchases and an additional 1% on the balance when paid off each statement period. If you purchase significant qualifying travel through Citi Travel, including hotels, rental cars, and attractions, the 5% cash-back could be a compelling reason to choose the Double Cash card. An important note: The card does not include travel insurance benefits to support those purchases. Redemptions When it’s time to redeem your rewards, you have several options with each card: SCROLL FOR MORE Redemption Double Cash Card Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Cash-back Statement credit, direct deposit to bank account, check Credit to a Wells Fargo credit card, checking account, or mortgage Cash via a Wells Fargo ATM Travel Travel through the Citi Travel portal, transfer to partners, transfer to premium Citi cards Cash-back for a statement credit to offset travel purchases Additional redemptions Gift cards, checkout with Amazon or PayPal, some retailers Gift cards, checkout with PayPal With the Double Cash card, you have the flexibility to transfer rewards to travel partners. However, the transfer ratio is not ideal, with 1,000 points equaling 700 airline miles, for example. Transferring points to a Citi premium card, such as the Citi Strata Premier® Card , results in higher redemption values. The Wells Fargo Active Cash card does not allow transfers to travel partners , but you can transfer rewards earned on the card to premium cards, such as the Wells Fargo Autograph Journey℠ Card , to use with Wells Fargo Rewards transfer partners . The cash rewards earned on either card have a base value of 1 cent each at redemption time and can easily be redeemed directly for cash. Balance Transfer and Purchase Offers Earning and redeeming rewards are important benefits of the Double Cash card and the Wells Fargo Active Cash card. However, the purchase and balance transfer offers on the cards can deliver extraordinary value for those with high-interest credit card debt or consumers who have large purchases coming up. A large purchase charged to the Wells Fargo Active Cash card could be paid off over time without interest charges. Image Credit: Ryan Smith Here is an overview of the introductory 0% APR offers on each card: SCROLL FOR MORE Benefit Double Cash Card Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Introductory 0% APR on balance transfers 0% intro APR on balance transfers for 18 months. After that, the variable APR will be 17.49% to 27.49%. 0% intro APR for 12 months from account opening on qualifying balance transfers. After that, your variable APR will be 18.49%, 24.49% or 28.49%. Balance transfers made within 120 days qualify for the intro rate and fee. Introductory 0% APR on purchases N/A 0% intro APR for 12 months from account opening on purchases. 18.49%, 24.49% or 28.49% Variable APR thereafter. Double Cash Card The Double Cash card offers an introductory 0% APR on balance transfers for 18 months when transfers are made within the first 4 months after card approval. If you have high-interest credit card balances (non-Citi cards), you can transfer them and repay them over time without incurring interest charges. After that, the variable APR is from 17.49% to 27.49%, depending on your creditworthiness. Balance transfers incur a 3% fee (minimum of $5) for transfers completed within the first 4 months and a 5% fee on each transfer after that (minimum $5). Terms apply. Wells Fargo Active Cash Card The introductory 0% APR for 12 months applies both to purchases and eligible balance transfers . Large purchases made with the card can be paid back over 12 months without incurring interest charges. Balance transfers must be made within 120 days from card approval to qualify for the 0% APR. After the 12-month 0% APR period has expired, a variable rate of 18.49%, 24.49%, or 28.49% applies, depending on your creditworthiness. The introductory 0% APR fee for balance transfers within the first 120 days is 3% or a minimum of $5, whichever is higher. After that, the transfer fee is 5% or a minimum of $5, whichever is higher. Bottom Line: Introductory 0% APR offers can save you money on interest rate charges. It’s important to pay off any qualifying purchases or balance transfers within the specified 0% APR period to avoid high interest rates applying to any unpaid balances. Travel Protections and Benefits The Double Cash card and Wells Fargo Active Cash card are not designed to function as travel rewards cards. In fact, both cards charge a 3% foreign transaction fee on the amount of any foreign purchase. However, each card offers a few useful protections and benefits. Book luxury hotels with your card for added benefits. Shangri-La Sydney. Image Credit: James Larounis Here are the useful travel protections and benefits on our featured cards: SCROLL FOR MORE Protection or Benefit Double Cash Card Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Rental car collision damage waiver N/A Secondary coverage in the U.S. Hotel benefits Mastercard Luxury Hotels & Resorts benefits Visa Signature Luxury Hotel Collection benefits Ride-share benefits $5 monthly Lyft credit after booking 3 or more Lyft rides N/A Roadside dispatch N/A A pay-per-use service Double Cash Card Mastercard Luxury Hotels & Resorts: Book with your card at over 3,000 properties worldwide and receive complimentary breakfast for 2 guests and an on-site amenity worth $100. Lyft ride credit : Use your card to book 3 or more Lyft rides in a month and receive a $5 Lyft credit. Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Automobile rental collision damage waiver: Pay for your rental car with your card, decline the agency’s CDW/LDW coverage, and receive secondary car rental coverage in the U.S. for up to 15 days and primary coverage outside the U.S. for up to 30 days. Visa Signature Luxury Hotel Collection : Receive room upgrades (when available), Wi-Fi, complimentary breakfast for 2 guests, a $25 food and beverage credit, VIP status, late checkout on request (when available), and a best-rate guarantee. You must use your card to book your stay. Roadside dispatch: Pay 1 set price for the service call, which includes limited towing, tire changes, jump-starts, lockout services, and emergency fuel. Limits apply. For more information on Wells Fargo Active Cash card benefits, access the benefits guide (Source: Wells Fargo ). Shopping Protections and Benefits There aren’t many shopping protections and benefits on the Double Cash card or the Wells Fargo Active Cash card. However, a few key protections and benefits can provide value: SCROLL FOR MORE Protection or Benefit Double Cash Card Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Cell phone protection N/A Up to $600 per claim, maximum $1,200 per 12 months Extended warranty 24 additional months N/A Shopping offers Citi Merchant Offers My Wells Fargo Deals Double Cash Card Extended warranty: For eligible items purchased with your card, with manufacturer’s warranties of 5 years or less, the warranty will be extended by 24 months. Citi Merchant Offers: Enroll in offers in your account and make the required purchase with your card to receive a statement credit. Wells Fargo Active Cash Card Cell phone protection: Pay for your monthly cell phone service with your card and receive up to $600 per claim for damage, involuntary and accidental parting, or theft. There is a $25 deductible per claim and a maximum of $1,200 or 2 claims per 12-month period. My Wells Fargo Deals: Get personalized cash-back offers for purchases at retailers and service providers. Final Thoughts The Double Cash card and the Wells Fargo Active Cash card each earn 2% cash-back . Additionally, the Double Cash card earns 5% cash-back on bonus categories such as hotels, car rentals, and attractions booked through Citi Travel. If you typically carry a card balance, you’d earn more on the Wells Fargo Active Cash card , as you would not receive the entire 2% on the Double Cash card (1% when making the purchase, 1% when paying the balance). The Wells Fargo Active Cash card is best for those who have large purchases they want to pay back over time using the introductory 0% APR for purchases . The Double Cash card is better for balance transfers because its introductory 0% APR period is 18 months , compared with 12 months on the Wells Fargo Active Cash card.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://baomoi.com/\",\"feedTitle\"