nk\":\"https://www.wsj.com/finance/fahmi-quadir-industry-assassin-3d6ccd82?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-24786519\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-18T00:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Carlotta Cardana for WSJ\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSMarketsMain\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: Markets\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"AI Chip Startup Etched Is in Talks for $20 Billion Valuation\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/ai-chip-startup-etched-is-in-talks-for-20-billion-valuation-caf1787d?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-62833332\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T23:42:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Etched\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=100003114\",\"feedTitle\":\"US Top News and Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Leather jacket worn by Nvidia CEO goes for just under $1 million at Sotheby's auction\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/17/leather-jacket-worn-by-nvidia-ceo-goes-for-just-under-1-million-at-sothebys-auction-.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F17%2Fleather-jacket-worn-by-nvidia-ceo-goes-for-just-under-1-million-at-sothebys-auction-.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T23:18:35.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The high price for the garment is a sign that collectors are looking to bid on artifacts and collectibles from the artificial intelligence boom.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"DGRO: A Buy As Capital Rotates Out Of Chips\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4923158-dgro-a-buy-as-capital-rotates-out-of-chips?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4923158-dgro-a-buy-as-capital-rotates-out-of-chips%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T23:15:54.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Is Citi Adding Japan Airlines as a Points Transfer Partner? Here’s What We Know.\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/citi-thankyou-transfer-japan-airlines-rumor/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/JFK-Japan-Airlines-A350-1000-banking.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T23:05:55.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"To be clear, nothing is confirmed, but it definitely looks like Citi is about to add Japan Airlines as a points transfer partner. Some cardmembers see an option to list their Mileage Bank loyalty program number on the ThankYou Points page — though transfers aren’t actually possible yet. This appears to be a strong indication that cardholders will soon be able to transfer ThankYou Points to Mileage Bank. Here’s what we know … and what we don’t. What We Know About Citi Transfers to Japan Airlines We know that not everyone is seeing this ; that’s the biggest thing to get out of the way. However, some customers with Citi ThankYou Points see an option to add their Japan Airlines Mileage Bank rewards number on Citi’s website. This was first spotted by several different users on Reddit . This is the same area where members can save their loyalty numbers for existing Citi transfer partners . Seeing an airline here that isn’t a transfer partner is highly abnormal, and it leads to an obvious rumor: that transfers to Japan Airlines are coming soon, and this accidentally appeared before it was supposed to . Image Credit: Citi Hot Tip: The addition of a new transfer partner wouldn’t be entirely surprising for Japan Airlines, which said earlier this year it wants to double the number of miles issued through partners and exchange programs. What We Don’t Know The list of things we don’t know is definitely longer than what we know at this point. First, we don’t know if this is really happening. We also don’t know when transfers will start , if that ever becomes a reality. Next, we don’t know what the transfer rate will be . Consider the varying transfer rates to Japan Airlines from different rewards programs: SCROLL FOR MORE Program Transfer Rate to JAL Mileage Bank Bilt Rewards 1:1 Capital One Miles 4:3 Marriott Bonvoy 3:1 Rove Miles 1:1 It could be any of these, or the transfer rate could be something different. Only time will tell. Final Thoughts It’s worth repeating that nothing is confirmed. We don’t know for sure whether Citi ThankYou Points will start transferring to Japan Airlines Mileage Bank, and we don’t know when the feature will go live — if ever. However, seeing Mileage Bank listed as an option to save your loyalty number, right next to where you save your number for Citi’s existing transfer partners, strongly suggests this will happen in the near future. We’ve reached out to Citi for a comment on this development. As of publication time, we haven’t heard back. If Citi provides any clarification about impending transfers, we’ll be sure to provide updates.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/chuyen-tro-linh-tinh-tm.17/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Chuyện trò linh tinh™