wner Taco Bell and the food distributor Sysco on Thursday to pull shredded lettuce that had been produced initially as 5-pound bags at a facility in Guanajuato, Mexico, from distribution. Taco Bell said on Thursday that \\\"The affected ingredient from our supplier is being indefinitely removed from our supply chain nationwide and will be replaced within 24 hours … Read the full story at The Verge.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=100727362\",\"feedTitle\":\"International: Top News And Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"The White House is dictating access to frontier AI models, shifting power from tech giants, sources say\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/17/white-house-ai-access-anthropic-openai.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F17%2Fwhite-house-ai-access-anthropic-openai.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T22:04:48.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The Trump administration is taking steps to control who gets access to the latest frontier models, people familiar with the matter told CNBC.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSMarketsMain\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: Markets\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"SpaceX and Pentagon Discuss Data-Center Deal\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/finance/stocks/spacex-and-pentagon-discuss-data-center-deal-23d0772f?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-64025778\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T21:46:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"ZUMAPRESS.com\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Earn up to 70K Atmos Rewards Points With Hawaiian Airlines Card’s New Offer\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/hawaiian-airlines-card-70k-bonus/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Hawaiian-Airlines-A321neo-takeoff-LAX.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T21:25:35.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The Hawaiian Airlines® World Elite Mastercard® is running one of its better welcome offers right now. New cardholders can earn up to 70,000 bonus Atmos Rewards points across the first several months. These points can cover flights to the islands and beyond, and fortunately, the spending bar to reach it is reasonable. Here’s how the bonus offer breaks down and whether the card earns its place in your wallet. New 70K Welcome Offer on the Hawaiian Airlines World Elite Card The new welcome bonus offer on the Hawaiian Airlines World Elite card comes in 2 parts . First, you’ll earn 60,000 Atmos Rewards points after spending $1,000 on purchases in the first 90 days from account opening. From there, you can earn an additional 10,000 points once you spend a total of $2,000 on purchases within the first 180 days. Hit both tiers, and you’ll get the the full 70,000 points. We value Atmos Rewards points at 1.6 cents each, which puts 70,000 points at roughly $1,120. The tiered structure gives you room to reach the full bonus offer without forcing a large amount of spending right away, so it works whether you charge a big purchase early or spread everyday spending across a few months. Applications are available here . Hot Tip: What can you do with this points after you earn them? These are our favorite ways to redeem Atmos Rewards points for top value . Hawaiian Airlines World Elite Card Benefits The card carries a $99 annual fee that is not waived during the first year, so the ongoing perks need to pull their weight — and they do. You’ll earn 3x Atmos Rewards points on eligible Hawaiian Airlines and Alaska Airlines purchases, 2x on gas, dining, and eligible grocery purchases, and 1x on everything else . That covers most everyday spending categories. Atmos Rewards points are useful for Alaska and Hawaiian flights, and for Oneworld partner tickets. Image Credit: Daniel Ross Cardholders get 2 free checked bags for you and eligible companions on the same Alaska or Hawaiian reservation, and that perk alone is most likely to cover the annual fee year after year. One round-trip for 2 easily offsets the $99, and a family trip clears it several times over. Because this is a travel card, you won’t pay any foreign transaction fees on purchases made outside the U.S. Final Thoughts With up to 70,000 points worth about $1,120 for travel, this welcome offer stands among the more rewarding airline credit card offers available today. Plus, the 2-tier structure keeps the spending requirement manageable for most everyday budgets. If you fly to Hawaii or lean on the Hawaiian and Alaska Airlines route networks, the free checked bag and ongoing earning make the card easy to justify well past the welcome bonus offer in the first year.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.morningstar.com/topics/stocks\",\"feedTitle\":\"Morningstar\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.morningstar.com/favicon.ico\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Kimi 3.0 Might Be a DeepSeek Moment; We’d Buy Several Cloud Computing Companies Malik Ahmed Khan, CFA J\",\"link\":\"https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/kimi-30-might-be-deepseek-moment-wed-buy-several-cloud-computing-companies\",\"image\":\"https://media.morningstar.com/resizer/v2/VGA7V5ORZ5HDZJBNP4B62NR7QY.jpg?auth=499642db27c10828a504a9831119a89eabd1546da2b23b96c2d0e57cbf06f5f3&quality=80&height=2400&width=2400&crop=525,0:1350,1350\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T21:17:19.469Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Kimi 3.0 Might Be a D