\":\"United Adds More Than 30 Flights Around Key College Football Games This Fall\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/united-airlines-routes-college-football-2026/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/United-Airlines-planes-parked-LAX.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T16:53:05.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Fall means different things to different people: apple cider, carving pumpkins, and United Airlines adding flights to help you follow your favorite college football team to its biggest road games. The carrier is back at it for the 2026 season, this time adding more than 30 new flights, flying bigger planes, and offering over 4,400 extra seats to get fans to top matchups across the country. That’s a noticeable jump from last year, and it shows this has become a real annual tradition for the airline. Additionally, United is also touting its Starlink Wi-Fi to help fans watch other games that might take place while they’re in the air. Let’s dig into the details. United Airlines Adds Flights for 2026 College Football Games Fans of Notre Dame, the Big Ten, and the SEC have the most to gain here. Like it did last year , United is crisscrossing the country to support marquee matchups involving teams like Notre Dame, Ohio State, Texas, Alabama, and Oregon, using a mix of brand-new routes and bigger planes on select flights. I recommend cheering for Ohio State, just FYI. Image Credit: Katie Corrigan Seemann Notre Dame gets the heaviest treatment, with added flights into South Bend (SBN) for a stretch of home games from September through November. However, the schedule spreads well beyond South Bend, hitting rivalry weekends and top-15 clashes from coast to coast. Here are the games United is adding flights for, along with the outbound and inbound options for each: SCROLL FOR MORE Matchup Outbound Flights Inbound Flights Notre Dame at Wisconsin (September 6) September 5: Newark (EWR) to Green Bay (GRB) September 6: Newark (EWR) to Green Bay (GRB) September 7: Green Bay (GRB) to Newark (EWR) Rice at Notre Dame (September 12) September 11: Houston (IAH) to South Bend (SBN) September 11: Newark (EWR) to South Bend (SBN) September 13: South Bend (SBN) to Houston (IAH) September 13: South Bend (SBN) to Newark (EWR) Ohio State at Texas (September 12) September 11: Columbus (CMH) to Austin (AUS) September 13: Austin (AUS) to Columbus (CMH) Michigan State at Notre Dame (September 19) September 18: Newark (EWR) to South Bend (SBN) September 20: South Bend (SBN) to Newark (EWR) Wisconsin at Penn State (September 26) September 25: Madison (MSN) to State College (SCE) September 27: State College (SCE) to Madison (MSN) Stanford at Notre Dame (October 10) October 9: Newark (EWR) to South Bend (SBN) October 9: San Francisco (SFO) to South Bend (SBN) October 11: South Bend (SBN) to Newark (EWR) October 11: South Bend (SBN) to San Francisco (SFO) Indiana at Nebraska (October 10) October 9: Indianapolis (IND) to Lincoln (LNK) October 11: Lincoln (LNK) to Indianapolis (IND) Alabama at Tennessee (October 17) October 16: Birmingham (BHM) to Knoxville (TYS) October 18: Knoxville (TYS) to Birmingham (BHM) Miami at Notre Dame (November 7) November 6: Newark (EWR) to South Bend (SBN) November 8: South Bend (SBN) to Newark (EWR) Alabama at LSU (November 7) November 6: Birmingham (BHM) to Baton Rouge (BTR) November 8: Baton Rouge (BTR) to Birmingham (BHM) Oregon at Ohio State (November 7) November 6: Eugene (EUG) to Columbus (CMH) November 8: Columbus (CMH) to Eugene (EUG) Texas at LSU (November 14) November 13: Austin (AUS) to Baton Rouge (BTR) November 15: Baton Rouge (BTR) to Austin (AUS) Boston College at Notre Dame (November 14) November 13: Newark (EWR) to South Bend (SBN) November 15: South Bend (SBN) to Newark (EWR) SMU at Notre Dame (November 21) November 20: Newark (EWR) to South Bend (SBN) November 22: South Bend (SBN) to Newark (EWR) Hot Tip: If any of these flights look pricey, keep in mind that paying with miles can help reduce the cost. It’s worth understanding how the United Airlines MileagePlus program works so you can redeem miles for these seats and save some cash for the tailgate. Final Thoughts United keeps building on this tradition, and the 2026 slate is its biggest college football push yet. The carrier has lined up more than 30 new flights, bigger planes on select routes, and over 4,400 added seats to get fans to the games that matter most. Plus, with the addition of free Starlink Wi-Fi for MileagePlus members , you can follow the scoreboard the whole way there.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/commodities.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Commodities Analysis & Opinion\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Gold’s Safe-Haven Role Is Breaking Under the Weight of Real Yields\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/golds-safehaven-role-is-breaking-under-the-weight-of-real-yields-200684152\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fgolds-safehaven-role-is-breaking-under-the-weight-of-real-yields-200684152&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T16:53:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Asus’ top-end 4K QD-OLED gaming monitor is $400 off\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/966907/asus-rog-swift-qd-oled-marathon-steam-deal-sale\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/asus-rog-swift-PG32UCDMR-roundup-2.png?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T16:47:13.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The discounted Asus QD-OLED in all its glory. | Image: The Verge The Asus ROG Swift 32-inch 4K QD-OLED gaming monitor has almost everything I want in a high-end gaming monitor, most notably a QD-OLED panel for inky black levels and vivid colors that go beyond what’s possible on an LCD screen. Amazon , Best Buy , and B&H Photo have this model on sale for $899.99 (usually $1,299.99). It’s particularly well-suited for fast-paced games with its 240Hz refresh rate, and G-Sync variable refresh rate to prevent screen tearing. This monitor has been available for this price for most of July. We’re not sure how long the deal will stick around for, but Asus is likely trying to move units at a discount so it can put more focus on its newer $1,299.99 model that has a Tandem QD-OLED display and slightly better specs. Asus ROG Swift OLED PG32UCDMR Where to Buy: $1299.99 $899.99 at Amazon $1299.99 $899.99 at Best Buy $1299.99 $899.99 at B&H Photo The port selection is good, comprised of a DisplayPort 2.1 input, a pair of HDMI 2.1 ports, and USB-C for video via DisplayPort alt mode (with 90W of charging power), plus a USB 3.2 Gen 1 hub with three Type-A ports. A unique feature is that this and several other Asus OLED monitors have a proximity sensor that let it turn off when you walk away to reduce the risk of burn-in. It has a three-year warranty that covers burn-in with normal use. Other deals to consider Newegg has Marathon for Steam on sale for $21.99 when you apply the coupon code EPF5365 at checkout. The notoriously difficult extraction shooter from Bungie is gorgeous and more inviting to new players in its second season that’s currently available. This is the cheapest price we’ve seen if you’re looking to start your career as a runner, and great timing ahead of the experimental PvE mode that’s launching on July 21st. A perennial favorite in our deal coverage, the Anker Nano Smart Display Charger Block is on sale for $25.99 at Best Buy and Amazon . The compact 45W USB-C power adapter with foldable prongs comes in four fun colors, and has a display on the front with charging progress and speed and a cute, smiley face to accompany you as your device charges. The Sennheiser Accentum Open Wireless Earbuds are $59.99 (usually $129.99) at Best Buy . They don’t have the same truly open design as other clip-on style earbuds like the Asus ROG Cetra Open Wireless , and instead fit in your ear without tips, similar to the standard Apple AirPods . They have an IPX4 rating, multipoint pairing, and up to 28 hours of runtime on a single charge, while still allowing outside noise to pass through. They’re a good, budget-friendly option if you’re looking for something to stay aware while working out or doing yardwork.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/stock.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Stock Markets Analysis & Opinion\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"GE Aerospace Faces a Prove-It Moment in Q2 Earnings\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/ge-aerospace-faces-a-proveit-moment-in-q2-earnings-200684150\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fge-aerospace-faces-a-proveit-moment-in-q2-earnings-200684150&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-17T16:39:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=100003114\",\"feedTitle\":\"US Top News and Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Tesla and Intel among stocks with earnings momentum reporting next week. Here are the others\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/17/tesla-and-intel-are-among-the-companies-reporting-next-week-with-positive-ear