ed for now.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"This Is Why I Prefer FLBR Over EWZ\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4922793-this-is-why-i-prefer-flbr-over-ewz?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4922793-this-is-why-i-prefer-flbr-over-ewz%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T22:46:05.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Point.me Adds Faster Searches, Multi-City Award Search, and New Redemption Tools\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/point-me-new-features-2026/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Uniteds-Premium-Boeing-789-Dreamliner-taking-off-from-London-Heathrow-Airport-LHR.jpeg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T22:30:08.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Searching for award flights can be one of the most time-consuming parts of booking a trip with points. Now, Point.me has introduced several new features aimed at speeding up and simplifying that process, including faster searches, multi-city searches, and new tools that help travelers find better redemption opportunities. If you regularly use Point.me to search for award flights, here’s what’s new and why it matters. What’s New in Point.me’s Latest Update? If you’re unfamiliar with Point.me , it’s an award search tool that helps travelers find flights they can book with points and miles. It searches live award availability across more than 150 airlines and dozens of loyalty and transferable rewards programs, then walks you through the booking process once you find an itinerary you like. Here’s a look at the biggest new features now rolling out to the platform. Find Award Flights Faster One of the biggest improvements is speed. Point.me says most award searches now load in under 20 seconds instead of taking close to a minute , making it much quicker to compare routes, airlines, or travel dates. Point.me searches should now load much faster than before. Image Credit: Point.me Another useful upgrade is multi-city search. Instead of searching 1 destination at a time, you can now search up to 3 origins and 3 destinations simultaneously for a specific travel date. For example, instead of searching Rome, Milan, and Venice separately, you can search all 3 cities at once and quickly compare which one offers the best redemption. It’s a simple change, but it can save a lot of time if you’re planning a trip and are open to multiple airports. Explore More Destinations If you’re flexible about where you want to travel, this feature may be the most useful addition. Premium members can now use Point.me’s revamped Explore tool to search for award opportunities based on the points they already have instead of starting with a specific destination. Point.me’s Explore tool map let’s you see dozens of destinations at once. Image Credit: Point.me You can narrow results by region, travel month, cabin, loyalty program, or even the maximum number of points you want to spend. There’s also a new calendar view that highlights the lowest-priced award dates, making it easier to spot the best deals without clicking through every day individually. That’s especially useful if your travel dates are flexible, since award prices can vary significantly from one day to the next. Get More Value From Your Points Point.me is also making it easier to maximize your transferable credit card points. The platform now displays active transfer bonuses directly in its search results, showing opportunities to book the same award for fewer points by transferring rewards from programs like American Express Membership Rewards , Chase Ultimate Rewards , Capital One miles , or Citi ThankYou Rewards . It also tells you when those transfer bonuses expire, so you know how long you have to take advantage of them. That’s a useful feature for anyone who books award travel regularly and doesn’t want to keep track of constantly changing transfer bonus offers. Another new addition is a built-in value indicator. Point.me now labels award flights as a “Good” or “Great” redemption after comparing the points price to the equivalent cash fare. While it shouldn’t replace your own judgment, it’s a helpful way to quickly identify award bookings that offer solid value for your points. A little badge on top of flight search result now tells you if you’re eyeing a “good” or “great” deal. Image Credit: Point.me Point.me also now displays the cash fare, the equivalent price through your credit card’s travel portal, and the transfer partner award price side by side in the search results. That makes it much easier to compare your options at a glance and quickly see whether transferring points offers better value than simply booking through your card’s travel portal or paying cash. Hot Tip: Award search tools can help you find available flights, but choosing the right transfer partner is just as important. Before moving your points, use our Transfer Partner Tool to compare airline and hotel partners and identify the best program for your redemption. Final Thoughts Award search tools are constantly evolving, and Point.me’s latest update brings several changes that frequent points travelers will likely appreciate. Faster searches, the ability to search multiple destinations at once, and built-in transfer bonus information all make it a little easier to find and compare award flights. Whether you’re already using Point.me or are simply keeping tabs on the latest award search tools, these are the key updates you’ll want to know before your next points redemption.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Delta Award Sale: Australia & New Zealand From 25K Miles Round-Trip [Book Today]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/delta-award-flash-sale/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Delta-Air-Lines-A330-300-Parked-ATL-Overview.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T22:23:21.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Delta just launched a new SkyMiles flash sale, and it’s a good one. With this award sale, you can book flights to Australia and New Zealand for as low as 30k SkyMiles round-trip — some of the lowest prices we have ever seen. But it gets even better: Delta SkyMiles co-branded credit cardholders can score an additional 15% off of those rates, bringing the total to just 25,400 miles. Here’s a look at what routes you can book, which were first noticed by Thrifty Traveler. Delta SkyMiles Flash Sale — The Details Delta Air Lines ‘ latest flash sale is valid for basic economy and Main Cabin tickets to Australia and New Zealand, starting at just 30,000 SkyMiles round-trip in basic economy. However, you can get these flights even cheaper — spending 15% fewer miles — if you hold a Delta co-branded credit card ! Here’s a look at the details: Class:  Basic economy and Main Cabin Routes:  Many U.S. cities to Auckland (AKL), Brisbane (BNE), and Sydney (SYD) Cost: From 30,000 miles round-trip in basic economy (or 15% fewer miles with an eligible Delta credit card) Travel dates:  September through December 2026 » Related: Delta Air Lines: Basic Economy vs. Main Cabin — What Are the Differences? How To Book This sale isn’t published on Delta’s SkyMiles Award Deals page , so you will need to run some manual searches to find the flight you are looking for. Fortunately, we are seeing availability from airports across the U.S., even smaller, regional airports. Delta’s award search feature is relatively easy to use. Just enter the route and dates you’re looking for, and select Shop with Miles and My Dates are Flexible then click Find Flights . This will bring up the Flexible Dates calendar, which will display the cheapest dates for the route you are looking for. Image Credit: Delta Air Lines From there, pick the dates that work best for you and follow the on-screen prompts to book your ticket. Image Credit: Delta Air Lines Note that if you have an eligible Delta co-branded credit card, you can save even more with the promo code TakeOff 15 . This perk provides a further discount during this award sale and will be shown automatically. If you need to earn more SkyMiles , you can transfer American Express Membership Rewards points at a 1:1 ratio . Transfers are typically instant. However, we don’t usually recommend transferring points to Delta since the program can charge astronomical rates for award seats. But with rates this low, it could make sense if you don’t have enough miles in your account. Hot Tip: Delta Amex cardholders can get 15% off award prices when redeeming Delta SkyMiles for Delta flights. It’s a quality benefit you can use as many times as you wish. Final Thoughts This latest SkyMiles flash sale is a great opportunity if you’ve been holding onto points and waiting for the right time to redeem them. With round-trip flights to Australia and New Zealand for 30,000 miles (or even less if you have a Delta co-branded credit card), you can stretch your balance further and still get solid value. Since there is no published date for this sale, it’s worth browsing the deals now. These limited-time rates tend to disappear fast once word gets out — and they’ll all be gone soon.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://tinhte.vn/rss/\",\"feedTitle\":\"Trang chủ\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=tinhte.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Cuộc đua thiết bị AI hậu smartphone: Humane AI, Rabbit R1 với lịch sử toàn những thất bại \\\"đẹp\\\"\",\"link\":\"https://tinhte.vn/thread/cuoc-dua-thiet-bi-ai-hau-smartphone-humane-ai-rabbit-r1-voi-lich-su-toan-nhung-that-bai-dep.4161139/\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ftinhte.vn%2Fthread%2Fcuoc-dua-thiet-bi-ai-hau-smartphone-humane-ai-rabbit-r1-voi-lich-su-toan-nhung-that-bai-dep.4161139%2F&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dtinhte.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T22:14:41.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Nếu xâu chuỗi lại những chiếc máy được quảng cáo là \\\"tương lai hậu-smartphone\\\" trong vài năm qua, có lẽ anh em sẽ thấy một điểm chung kỳ lạ: gần như chiếc nào cũng chết theo cùng một kịch bản. Ra mắt hoành tráng, được vài tạp chí công nghệ gọi là phát minh của năm, rồi vài tháng sau xuất hiện hàng loạt đánh giá tiêu cực, và cuối cùng lặng lẽ bị khai tử hoặc bán tháo tài sản. Rồi giờ đến lượt OpenAI bước vào canh bạc này khi vài hôm gần đây tin đồn startup này ra mắt một thiết bị loa AI không... Cuộc đua thiết bị AI hậu smartphone: Humane AI, Rabbit R1 với lịch sử toàn những thất bại \\\"đẹp\\\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"QQQJ: The Structure Keeps Handing Its Winners To QQQ\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4922787-qqqj-the-structure-keeps-handing-its-winners-to-qqq?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F492