ll,\"content\":\"The streaming giant said it would cut back on the frequency of its \\\"What We Watched\\\" reports, which provide a picture of engagement.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"IAUI: Monthly Income Helps In A Range-Bound Gold Market, But NAV Erosion Keeps It A Hold\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4922785-iaui-monthly-income-helps-in-a-range-bound-gold-market-but-nav-erosion-keeps-it-a-hold?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4922785-iaui-monthly-income-helps-in-a-range-bound-gold-market-but-nav-erosion-keeps-it-a-hold%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T21:45:08.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSMarketsMain\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: Markets\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Here’s What Is Happening Behind the Market’s Swings, in Charts\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/finance/stocks/heres-what-is-happening-behind-the-markets-swings-in-charts-a88fef3f?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-16985793\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T21:41:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Uncredited\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Fortnite is getting a bunch of AI-powered ‘personas’\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/games/966815/epic-games-fortnite-ai-powered-personas\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/uefn-conversations-blog-header-opt-02.jpeg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T21:31:58.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Get ready for more AI characters in Fortnite . Developer Epic Games is going to let Fortnite creators publish experiences featuring characters with AI-powered voices starting on July 30th, and ahead of that launch, it's created 36 characters with \\\"consistent voices and personas\\\" that creators can use as NPCs. The characters include Fortnite staples like Agent Jonesy, Peely ( the banana ), Fishstick (a walking fish), and Cuddle Team Leader (who wears a pink bear mascot head). Epic tested the waters of AI characters with last year's Darth Vader NPC that was powered by James Earl Jones' voice - a collaboration that Jones' estate signed off on . Ev … Read the full story at The Verge.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Making Sense of US Consumer Price Indexes, Jobs Numbers and Sentiment Surveys\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-16/making-sense-of-us-consumer-price-indexes-jobs-numbers-and-sentiment-surveys\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-16%2Fmaking-sense-of-us-consumer-price-indexes-jobs-numbers-and-sentiment-surveys&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T20:57:54.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"On today’s Big Take podcast: We take stock of the US economy — what the latest data tell us, and what it misses about Americans’ financial reality.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSWorldNews\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: World News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Saudi Arabia Was in the Midst of Transformation. Then Came the Iran War.\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-riyadh-iran-war-99434d4b\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-33182388\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T20:48:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Hamad I Mohammed/Reuters\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Samsung’s 55-inch Frame art TV is $200 cheaper than usual\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/966613/samsung-the-frame-art-tv-deal-sale\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/04/samsungtheframetv75inch.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T20:47:30.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Samsung’s art TV looks right at home alongside real paintings. | Image: Samsung Samsung’s Frame is different from your average 4K TV. Its biggest selling point involves what it does when you aren’t actively using it. It can display art, turning your living room into a gallery. The Frame has bezels that make it look like — you guessed it — framed art, and its matte finish can replicate paintings more naturally than your typical glossy-coated TV. Amazon currently has the 55-inch Samsung Frame on sale for $697.99, about $200 lower than its typical price. The deal is on the 2025 model that features a 4K QLED panel, 144Hz refresh rate with variable refresh rate, and HDR10 Plus support. Samsung The Frame (2025) Where to Buy: $899.99 $697.99 at Amazon (55-inch) $899.99 $699.99 at Best Buy $1697.99 $897.99 at Woot (65-inch) The Frame connects with a single cable to its included One Connect box, which contains a bunch of inputs. The box has four HDMI ports (two that support 4K at 60Hz, one with eARC for soundbars, and one that supports 4K at 144Hz for gaming), two USB-A ports, a coaxial plug for an HD antenna, Ethernet, and optical audio. Like other art TVs , the Frame underperforms in a handful of ways that might matter to you compared to other similarly-priced TVs. Our analysis of the Frame and its competitors showed that they generally have lower maximum brightness, lackluster picture quality and color accuracy, and poorer black levels, all of which can have a negative impact on how movies, TV shows and games look. Despite its drawbacks, the Frame might be a nice compromise between dominating your living room with a TV or hanging up a painting.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/302.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Cryptocurrency Opinion & Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Bitcoin Leverage Is Rising Faster Than Spot Demand Can Absorb\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/bitcoin-leverage-is-rising-faster-than-spot-demand-can-absorb-200684088\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fbitcoin-leverage-is-rising-faster-than-spot-demand-can-absorb-200684088&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T20:34:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/286.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Most Popular Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Imagining the Unthinkable for AI Investors\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysi