pinion\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Silver’s Supply Deficit Faces a New Layer of North American Trade Risk\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/silvers-supply-deficit-faces-a-new-layer-of-north-american-trade-risk-200684085\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fsilvers-supply-deficit-faces-a-new-layer-of-north-american-trade-risk-200684085&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T19:41:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"RISR: Upgrading This Negative-Duration ETF As Inflation Fears Return\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4922762-risr-upgrading-this-negative-duration-etf-as-inflation-fears-return?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4922762-risr-upgrading-this-negative-duration-etf-as-inflation-fears-return%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T19:33:01.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10001147\",\"feedTitle\":\"Business News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"UnitedHealth blows past estimates, hikes earnings outlook as it reins in costs\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/unitedhealth-group-unh-earnings-q2-2026.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Funitedhealth-group-unh-earnings-q2-2026.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:37.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The healthcare giant is working to stabilize margins by shrinking membership, exiting unprofitable contracts and pouring $1.5 billion into AI.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Buy Air Canada Aeroplan Points With up to a 110% Bonus [Until August 12]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/buy-aeroplan-points-with-bonus/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Air-Canada-A330-300-at-YUL.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:51:33.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Air Canada is currently running a limited-time promotion on purchased Aeroplan points, with eligible members seeing up to a 110% bonus through August 12, 2026 . At the top advertised rate, the cost drops to roughly 1.33 cents per Aeroplan point, which is below our current valuation of these points. Just note that offers are targeted, so your bonus may vary during this current promotion. Let’s look at the details and decide whether you should hop on this promotion. Air Canada’s Latest Buy Aeroplan Points Promotion Whether you’re topping up your Aeroplan account balance or have found a redemption that makes buying points cheaper than paying for the flight in cash, this promotion could be helpful in the right situation. Air Canada is currently running a limited-time promotion on Aeroplan points purchased through August 12, 2026, with most members receiving a 100% bonus and eligible Aeroplan® Credit Card holders receiving an additional 10% bonus. If you have the 110% offer, you’ll see the following multitiered offer when buying Aeroplan points: Buy up to 4,000 points without a bonus. Buy 5,000 to 25,000 points with a 60% bonus. Buy 30,000 to 80,000 points with a 80% bonus. Buy 90,000+ points with a 110% bonus (1.33 cents each). Direct link to purchase Note that there’s a limit of 500,000 purchased points per transaction . Keep in mind that Aeroplan also has targeted offers on point purchases, so your offer may differ. If you have the 110% bonus offer and purchase the maximum of 500,000 points, you’ll pay CA$18,750 ($13,333) to take home 1 million points in this sale. That’s a per-point cost of 1.33 cents. We value Air Canada Aeroplan points at 1.5 cents apiece, so this sale comes in below that valuation. Hot Tip: Buying points from Aeroplan won’t count as an airfare purchase on your credit card because Points.com processes sales. To maximize your earnings, use a good credit card for everyday purchases , or a card you’re spending on to earn a welcome offer . Why You May Want To Purchase Aeroplan Points Here are the 2 main situations in which we think buying points and miles is valuable: You don’t have enough transferable points (e.g., Amex Membership Rewards , Bilt Rewards , Capital One Miles , Chase Ultimate Rewards , and Rove Miles ) or Aeroplan points to make the booking you want. Buying points to make a redemption costs less than paying for the flight outright. Consider this: Purchasing 210,000 Aeroplan points under this promotion with a 110% bonus (at 1.33 cents each) would set you back roughly $2,793 — certainly not a small sum of cash. However, you could redeem those 210,000 points to  fly round-trip in  Lufthansa first class  between the U.S. and Europe . You can book Lufthansa’s first class with Aeroplan points. Image Credit: Cherag Dubash Lufthansa first-class tickets often cost $8,000 or more, so purchasing points could save you more than 65% when compared to the standard cash fare ! Hot Tip: Discover even more ways to redeem Aeroplan points for maximum value. Final Thoughts It doesn’t always make sense to purchase points or miles. Usually, earning points from welcome bonuses and daily spending on credit cards makes more sense. However, if your mileage balance is looking bare and you have an immediate use for these Aeroplan points, purchasing during this promotion might make sense — and it could save you a lot of cash in the process if you have your eye on a flight in a premium cabin. It may also make sense if the cash price of your flight is high and purchasing the required Aeroplan points comes out cheaper. If that’s the case, you have until August 12 to take advantage of this promotion, with eligible members seeing up to a 110% bonus.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Dallas Fed President Logan calls for 'modestly' higher interest rates\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/dallas-fed-president-logan-calls-for-modestly-higher-interest-rates.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Fdallas-fed-president-logan-calls-for-modestly-higher-interest-rates.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:50:42.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The policymaker said this week's good inflation news wasn't good enough.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Kalshi says it caught Trump’s teleprompter operator insider trading\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/news/966676/trump-teleprompter-operator-kalshi-bets-mention-markets-investigation\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/02/STKB383_KALSHI_A.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:43:14.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Kalshi users betting on what President Donald Trump would say during his speeches were reportedly up against tough competition: the president's teleprompter operator. ABC News reports that federal investigators believe Gabriel Perez - Trump's teleprompter operator since 2016 - used inside information to make bets on Kalshi, a major prediction market platform that allows users to bet on just about everything. One category that Kalshi offers is \\\"mentions\\\" markets, in which users try to predict what an individual will say during high-profile events. Perez is accused of betting on what Trump would say during more than a dozen events, including … Read the full story at The Verge.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"South Africa Eyes $46 Billion for Industrial Hubs by April\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-16/south-africa-targets-46-billion-for-industrial-hubs-by-april\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-16%2Fsouth-africa-targets-46-billion-for-industrial-hubs-by-april&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:34:52.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"South Africa plans to attract billions of dollars in investment into its specialized industrial hubs by April to help revive a manufacturing sector that’s been in decline for decades.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"[Award Alert] New SWISS Senses Business Class Has Wide-Open Awards From 60K Points\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/award-alert-swiss-senses-business-class/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Swiss-Senses-Business-Class-Seat.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:28:26.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The new SWISS Senses business class is finally bookable with points. Better yet, the airline’s new Airbus A350 — currently operating only between Boston (BOS) and Zurich (ZRH) in the U.S. — has award space available. We’re seeing availability for up to a whopping 9 passengers from Boston to Zurich between January and March 2027 , while return flights from Zurich to Boston are available from July to September 2026 and again in April and May 2027. You can book these flights for just 60,000 points each way . Let’s check out the details. SWISS Senses Award Alert Details Thanks to our savvy LEVEL UP Travel Facebook community, we spotted wide-open award space for up to 9 passengers on SWISS ‘ new Airbus A350 featuring the airline’s new Senses business class , and we were able to confirm the availability through Air Canada Aeroplan . If you’re already planning a European vacation or simply looking for an affordable way home after spending time abroad, the return availability this summer could be especially valuable. Class: Business (SWISS Senses) Booking program: Air Canada Aeroplan Airline: SWISS Route: Boston (BOS) to Zurich (ZRH) Cost: 60,000 Aeroplan points plus CA$80 (about $57) in taxes and fees Travel dates: July to September 2026, January to March 2027, and April to May 2027 Award seats: Up to 9 passengers To ensure you’re flying the new Senses product, you’ll want to search for flights from Boston (BOS) to Zurich (ZRH) between January and March 2027 . In the opposite direction, we’re finding numerous dates from July through September 2026 and again in April and May 2027 . You can use a tool like Seats.aero to search numerous dates at once and then head to Aeroplan to book once you’ve found something you like. Image Credit: Seats.aero This is one of the first opportunities we’ve seen to easily book SWISS’ newest premium product with points, making it an exciting redemption for aviation enthusiasts and anyone planning a trip to Switzerland or heading back home to the U.S. » Related: Best Ways To Book SWISS Business Class With Points [Step by Step] How To Book You’ll want to book through Aeroplan, where nonstop SWISS Senses flights will cost 60,000 points plus a nominal amount of taxes and fees at approximately $57 . Image Credit: Aeroplan While many flights have up to 2 business class award seats available, we’re also seeing select dates with as many as 9 seats bookable in business class — something that’s almost unheard of on a brand-new premium cabin. If you’re traveling with family or a group of friends, this is a fantastic opportunity to book everyone on the same flight. One of the best things about booking through Aeroplan is how easy it is to earn the points. You can transfer points at a 1:1 ratio from Amex Membership Rewards , Bilt Rewards , Capital One miles , Chase Ultimate Rewards , and Rove Miles to Air Canada Aeroplan at a 1:1 rate. Plus, you can transfer from Marriott Bonvoy at a 3:1 ratio if you’re in a pinch. Hot Tip: We’ve been keeping a close eye on award space for SWISS’ new Senses business class ever since the Boston route launched, and this is the first time we’ve seen availability this wide open. If experiencing SWISS’ newest flagship cabin is on your bucket list, you may want to run — not walk — to book before these seats disappear. Final Thoughts Getting the chance to fly a brand-new business-class product shortly after it enters service is rare, especially at just 60,000 points each way. If SWISS Senses has been on your radar, now is a great time to book. Whether you’re heading to Switzerland or looking for a comfortable ride home from Europe, these awards offer an excellent opportunity to experience SWISS’ newest flagship cabin without paying cash.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"FRDM: All You Need To Know About This Niche EM ETF\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4922734-frdm-all-you-need-to-know-about-niche-em-etf?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4922734-frdm-all-you-need-to-know-about-niche-em-etf%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:17:33.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"IVE: Value Stocks Hit An All-Time High, Why Investors Should Stick With The Style\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4922732-ive-value-stocks-hit-an-all-time-high-why-investors-should-stick-with-the-style?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4922732-ive-value-stocks-hit-an-all-time-high-why-investors-should-stick-with-the-style%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:17:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Short sellers load up against SpaceX as stock drops below IPO price\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/short-sellers-load-up-against-spacex-as-stock-retreats-back-to-ipo-price.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Fshort-sellers-load-up-against-spacex-as-stock-retreats-back-to-ipo-price.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T18:12:21.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"About 185 million SpaceX shares are now sold short, representing roughly 29% of the company's publicly tradable float, according to S3.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"New York governor says she’s using AI to analyze ‘every single rule’ in the state\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/966647/new-york-governor-kathy-hochul-ai-policies\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/gettyimages-2283395662.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T17:58:37.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"New York Governor Kathy Hochul might have just signed a moratorium on new AI data centers in the state, but she's not against using the technology herself. During an interview with Bloomberg 's Odd Lots podcast, Hochul said that her team is using \\\"AI to analyze every single rule, regulation, [and] policy\\\" to check for outdated legislation. Some of the antiquated laws mentioned by Hochul in the interview include a $25 fee required to take a dog hunting, or a stipulation that pregnant people need a permit to work after midnight. Hochul added that it \\\"probably would have taken five years at the staff level\\\" to review all of the laws in the stat … Read the full story at The Verge.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.theverge.com/rss/index.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"The Verge\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.theverge.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"Ecovacs’ self-cleaning Deebot X11 has hit a new low price\",\"link\":\"https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/966651/ecovacs-deebot-x11-robot-vacuum-deal-sale\",\"image\":\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/ecovacsomnicyclone11deebots.webp?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T17:57:15.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Sometimes it feels like keeping your floors clean is one of those never-ending chores, which is why it's nice to have a versatile robot vacuum take it off your hands. The Ecovacs Deebot X11 robovac / mop hybrid is designed to do just that, and it's now $699 ($400 off) at Amazon and directly from Ecovacs , which is a new low price. The Deebot X11 is the latest version of one of our former top picks for the best robot vacuum / mop. While the Matic has since taken its place in our rankings, the X11 remains an excellent option, especially at nearly half the price. It combines powerful 19,500Pa suction along with a handful of features that make … Read the full story at The Verge.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Fed’s Schmid Says Inflation Too Hot, Above Target Too Long\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-16/fed-s-schmid-says-inflation-is-too-hot-above-target-too-long\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-16%2Ffed-s-schmid-says-inflation-is-too-hot-above-target-too-long&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T17:25:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City President Jeff Schmid said inflation is his biggest worry given the risk of a further acceleration in the months ahead.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"House Passes Bill That Could Bring More Family TSA Lanes to U.S. Airports\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/tsa-family-security-lane-bill/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/TSA-standard-Precheck-Clear-lanes-MCO-Terminal-B.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T17:24:10.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Traveling with young kids is stressful enough without juggling strollers, diaper bags, and restless children in a crowded TSA checkpoint. A newly introduced Senate bill aims to make that experience a little easier by requiring TSA to create dedicated security lanes for families traveling with children. Here’s what travelers need to know. New Bill Would Require TSA To Create Family Security Lanes If you’ve traveled internationally with young children, this concept may sound familiar. I’ve flown with my family all over the world, and in several countries outside the U.S., security officers have spotted us pushing a stroller and simply waved us into a separate lane. More than once, an agent has even opened an entirely new screening lane just to help families move through security faster. It’s a small gesture, but when you’re traveling with young kids, it makes a huge difference. That kind of treatment is rare in the U.S., but a new proposal in Congress could change that. Senators introduced the Families Fly Fairly Act , legislation that would require the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) to establish dedicated family screening lanes at airport security checkpoints . If you’ve ever navigated a busy TSA PreCheck line with a baby in a stroller, you know just how much a dedicated family security lane could help. Image Credit: Juan Ruiz Under the proposal, airports would be required to provide designated screening lanes for passengers traveling with children under 13 whenever it’s operationally feasible. The bill also directs TSA to develop policies aimed at reducing wait times and making the screening process easier for families. The legislation comes as air travel continues to see record demand, with long security lines becoming a common frustration during busy travel periods. For parents traveling with toddlers, strollers, car seats, formula, and carry-on bags, even a relatively short wait can quickly become overwhelming. Currently, there is no nationwide TSA policy requiring family screening lanes . If approved, the bill could expand the program beyond the handful of airports that already offer dedicated screening lanes, giving more families access to them. It’s worth noting that this is only proposed legislation. The bill must still move through Congress before anything changes at TSA checkpoints. Hot Tip: If you have TSA PreCheck, children ages 12 and younger can accompany an enrolled parent or guardian through the PreCheck lane at no additional cost. If you haven’t enrolled yet, check out our guide to TSA PreCheck and Global Entry to learn how the programs work and take a glance at our recommended cards that will reimburse the application fee for TSA PreCheck . Final Thoughts Nothing has changed yet, as the bill must still pass the Senate before becoming law. Even then, TSA would have the option — not a requirement — to launch the pilot program. Still, it’s a positive step for families. If TSA expands dedicated family lanes beyond the handful of airports that already offer them, parents could spend less time in security lines and more time enjoying their trip.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"New Welcome Bonus Offer on the World of Hyatt Business Card: Earn 70K Points\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/world-of-hyatt-business-card-offer-70k-points/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Hyatt-Centric-Delfina-Santa-Monica-bed-from-window.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T17:20:46.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"For anyone who’s been looking for a way to boost their World of Hyatt points balance, this one is worth a look. The World of Hyatt Business Credit Card is currently has a higher-than-usual welcome offer of 70,000 points. We’ll break down the details of this offer and the card’s key features so you can decide whether it deserves a spot in your wallet. Elevated World of Hyatt Business Card Welcome Offer For a limited time, you can earn a higher welcome offer bonus on the World of Hyatt Business card . Qualifying applicants can earn 70,000 bonus points after spending $7,000 on purchases within the first 3 months of account opening. For comparison, the card’s standard offer is 60,000 points after you spend $5,000 on purchases within the same window. The current offer asks for more spending, but it also delivers more points. Since we value World of Hyatt points at 1.4 cents each, those 70,000 points come out to roughly $980, which is a healthy return. Hot Tip: Once you’ve stacked up all those points, you need a plan for spending them. Take a look at our guide to the best ways to redeem World of Hyatt points for maximum value for ideas. World of Hyatt Business Card: Overview Beyond the welcome offer, the World of Hyatt Business card holds its own thanks to a solid rewards rate and a lineup of useful perks. This one could be worth shelling out for. Image Credit: Andrey Popov via Adobe Stock modified by Upgraded Points LLC Here’s how you earn points : 4 points per $1 spent on Hyatt stays 2 points per $1 spent on your top 3 eligible spending categories each quarter, including these categories: airline tickets purchased directly with the airline; car rental agencies; gas stations; dining; internet, cable, and phone services; public transit and commuting; shipping; and social media and search engine advertising 2 points per $1 spent at fitness clubs and on gym memberships 1 point per $1 spent on all other purchases The card also comes with a set of benefits that stand out, starting with World of Hyatt Discoverist elite status . That status unlocks perks like room upgrades when available, late checkout when available, a 10% bonus on points earned, and more. There’s more to like, too. Cardholders receive up to $100 in Hyatt statement credits every calendar year (available as 2 separate $50 statement credits), 5 World of Hyatt elite-qualifying nights for every $10,000 spent on the card in a calendar year, a 10% rebate on all the points you redeem for the rest of the year after spending $50,000 on the card, travel and purchase protections, and more. » Related: 13 Valuable Benefits of the World of Hyatt Business Credit Card [2026] Final Thoughts If you run a small business and find yourself booking Hyatt properties on a regular basis, this 70,000-point welcome offer makes it a good time to consider the World of Hyatt Business card. On top of the offer, the card’s earning structure and roster of benefits give you even more reason to put your Hyatt stays and daily business spending on it.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Warren Buffett calls Bill Gates' actions with Epstein 'distasteful' but says people make mistakes\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/warren-buffett-calls-bill-gates-actions-with-epstein-distasteful-but-people-make-mistakes.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Fwarren-buffett-calls-bill-gates-actions-with-epstein-distasteful-but-people-make-mistakes.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T17:07:36.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The Berkshire Hathaway chairman left out the Gates Foundation from his annual charitable stock gifts for the first time in 20 years.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSWorldNews\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: World News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Chevron Will Explore Creating Strait of Hormuz Alternative for Iraqi Oil\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/chevron-will-explore-creating-strait-of-hormuz-alternative-for-iraqi-oil-36308abf\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-26536667\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:48:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Graeme Sloan/POOL/EPA/Shutterstock\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/286.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Most Popular Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Netflix Earnings Preview: 5 Things Investors Need to Watch\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/netflix-earnings-preview-5-things-investors-need-to-watch-200684070\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fnetflix-earnings-preview-5-things-investors-need-to-watch-200684070&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:41:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Sen. Warren says Trump's CFPB overhaul has cost Americans $26.5 billion\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/trumps-cfpb-overhaul-cost-americans-26point5-billion-sen-warren-says.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Ftrumps-cfpb-overhaul-cost-americans-26point5-billion-sen-warren-says.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:36:23.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Sen. Elizabeth Warren says the Trump administration's rollback of CFPB rules and enforcement has cost Americans up to $26.5 billion so far.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"New Amex Offer: Get $100 Back After Spending $500 or More at Relais & Chateaux [Targeted]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/amex-offer-relais-chateaux/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Auberge-du-Soleil-Relais-Chateaux.webp\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:24:45.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"If you have an American Express card, or more than one, check your accounts because there’s a new Amex Offer floating around that could save you money on a high-end hotel stay. Not everyone will be able to take advantage of this offer because it’s targeted to specific accounts, but if you have travel coming up and want to stay at a luxurious property, it’s worth checking to see if you have it. Here’s everything you need to know. Relais & Chateaux Amex Offer — The Details From now through November 15, 2026, you can earn a $100 statement credit after spending $500 or more on room rates and room charges at participating Relais & Chateaux properties worldwide . Save money on an upcoming Relais & Chateaux stay. Screenshot: American Express Note that stays must be booked online at relaischateaux.com or by phone at 800-735-2478. This offer isn’t valid for purchases made through third parties , and qualifying purchases must total $500 after foreign currency conversion. If you’re not familiar, Relais & Chateaux is an independent collection of almost 600 hotels and restaurants spanning 65 countries worldwide . Member properties are largely high-end and emphasize their local setting, high standards of service, and an incredible gastronomic experience. There are 96 Relais & Chateaux hotels and restaurants located in the U.S., with hundreds more across the world, so no matter where your travels take you, there’s a good chance you’ll be able to find a location at which to use this offer. Plus, many properties — especially those in the U.S. — have starting room rates of well over $500, so you should have no problem meeting the terms of this offer once you zero in on a property. What Are Amex Offers? Amex Offers let you get more out of your American Express purchases, whether you earn Membership Rewards points or a statement credit, as with this Relais & Châteaux offer. However, Amex Offers are not automatically loaded to your card;  you have to add them manually . Also, keep in mind that many offers are targeted. That means while you may see an offer on 1 Amex card, you may not see the same offer on another. It seems this particular offer is broadly targeted, so if you have an Amex card, or multiple, there’s no reason not to check if you have it. Hot Tip: To learn more, check out our list of the best Amex Offers available right now. Final Thoughts If you have travel coming up and want to splurge on a fancy hotel for a night or 2, this is a great opportunity to earn cash-back on a Relais & Chateaux stay. Remember, purchases must be completed before November 15, 2026, to be eligible.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/290.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Editor's Picks\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"8 Undervalued Stocks That Fit Warren Buffett’s Value Investing Playbook\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/8-undervalued-stocks-that-fit-warren-buffetts-value-investing-playbook-200684032\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2F8-undervalued-stocks-that-fit-warren-buffetts-value-investing-playbook-200684032&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:11:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=19832390\",\"feedTitle\":\"Asia News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Nvidia unveils new AI model and expands Japan’s physical AI ecosystem\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/nvidia-reveals-new-ai-model-and-expands-japans-physical-ai-ecosystem.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Fnvidia-reveals-new-ai-model-and-expands-japans-physical-ai-ecosystem.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:08:29.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Nvidia announces new AI model, Cosmos 3 Edge, and expansion of its physical AI ecosystems in Japan.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Stocks making the biggest moves midday: Manpower, Abbott, UnitedHealth, TSMC & more\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/stocks-making-the-biggest-moves-midday-man-abt-unh-tsm-more.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Fstocks-making-the-biggest-moves-midday-man-abt-unh-tsm-more.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T16:06:13.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"These are the stocks posting the largest moves in midday trading.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Nigeria Expects Remittances to Hit $1 Billion a Month by Year-End\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-16/nigeria-expects-remittances-to-hit-1-billion-a-month-by-year-end\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-16%2Fnigeria-expects-remittances-to-hit-1-billion-a-month-by-year-end&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T15:41:31.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Nigeria anticipates remittances from citizens living abroad to increase by two-thirds over 2026 as it seeks to bolster its foreign-exchange reserves, its central bank governor said.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"IMF Cautions Burnham Against Raising UK’s Top Income Tax Rate\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-16/imf-cautions-burnham-against-raising-uk-s-top-income-tax-rate\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-16%2Fimf-cautions-burnham-against-raising-uk-s-top-income-tax-rate&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T15:30:17.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The International Monetary Fund has warned incoming UK prime minister Andy Burnham that raising the top rate of income tax would hurt the economy by discouraging work, and recommended higher rates on the lower paid instead.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.bloomberg.com/economics/news.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Bloomberg Economics\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=feeds.bloomberg.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Fed’s Watchdog Warns On Insider Risk after China Secrets Case\",\"link\":\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-07-16/fed-s-watchdog-warns-on-insider-risk-after-china-secrets-case\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bloomberg.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2F2026-07-16%2Ffed-s-watchdog-warns-on-insider-risk-after-china-secrets-case&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dfeeds.bloomberg.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T15:04:42.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The Federal Reserve’s internal watchdog warned Thursday the central bank needs to do more to protect sensitive economic information that is being pursued by foreign adversaries.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSWorldNews\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: World News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Yohei Kono, Who Apologized for Japan’s Role in Sex Slavery During World War II, Dies at 89\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/world/asia/japan-yohei-kono-dies-politician-b32fe623\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-95415452\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T15:03:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"KAZUHIRO NOGI/Agence France-Presse/Getty Images\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Buy Avianca Lifemiles With up to a 130% Bonus [Until July 24]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/buy-avianca-lifemiles-bonus/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/Avianca-B787-at-BOG-airport.png\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T14:35:54.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Avianca Lifemiles is a useful program for booking award tickets with Star Alliance carriers like United Airlines, Lufthansa, Turkish Airlines, and more. It’s also a favorite because it doesn’t tack on hefty fees to your award bookings. While a 130% bonus certainly makes this promotion more appealing than buying miles at the standard rate, that doesn’t automatically mean it’s a great deal. Whether it’s worth taking advantage of depends on how you plan to use those miles. So, is this promotion actually worth it? Let’s break it down. How To Purchase Avianca Lifemiles With up to a 130% Bonus Through July 24, 2026 , at 11:59 p.m. CST, you’ll earn a bonus when purchasing Avianca Lifemiles , and the bonus is available in 3 tiers: Buy 1,000 to 20,000 miles with a 115% bonus Buy 21,000 to 50,000 miles with a 120% bonus Buy 51,000 to 200,000 miles with a 130% bonus (1.43 cents each) Direct link to purchase With the 130% bonus, you could spend $6,600 to buy 200,000 miles — the maximum allowed in a single transaction — and come away with 460,000 miles in the end. That equates to 1.43 cents per mile . Image Credit: Lifemiles We value Avianca Lifemiles at 1.4 cents apiece, meaning you’d be buying miles for just above our estimated value. As a result, this promotion is best suited for travelers who have a specific redemption in mind. Keep in mind that you’re limited to purchasing a maximum of 500,000 miles per calendar year  before any bonuses are added. Hot Tip: Since Avianca purchases are processed by points.com, they won’t count as an airfare purchase on your credit card. That means you should use your best credit card for everyday spending , or use this purchase toward a credit card with a solid welcome bonus right now. How To Redeem Lifemiles For the right redemption, purchasing LifeMiles through this promotion can translate into substantial savings on your next flight. Better yet, those miles can be redeemed on a wide range of Star Alliance airlines. Here are a couple of compelling options: Fly business class to Europe: You can book a one-way business class ticket to Europe with multiple Star Alliance airlines like SWISS, Turkish Airlines, Brussels Airlines, and more for 70,000 to 80,000 miles , depending on the route. If you buy miles at 1.43 cents apiece during this promotion, you could purchase enough miles for $1,056 or $1,221 — a great price considering these kinds of tickets typically run for thousands of dollars one-way. Fly transcontinental in the U.S. on United Polaris: You can book a one-way United business class award from Newark (EWR) to Los Angeles (LAX) or San Francisco (SFO) for 25,000 Lifemiles. If you buy Lifemiles at 1.43 cents apiece right now, you could purchase the miles needed to book the ticket for $396 . This is a pretty stellar price, given that typical cash prices for these cross-country flights range between $1,200 and $3,000 one-way. Turkish Airlines business class on the Boeing 787-9. Image Credit: Juan Ruiz Avianca is also a transfer partner of 7 major reward currencies. If you have points or miles with  Amex Membership Rewards ,  Bilt Rewards ,  Brex Rewards ,  Capital One miles ,  Citi ThankYou Rewards ,  Marriott Bonvoy , or  Wells Fargo Rewards , you’ll want to consider transferring points from one of these programs first to lower your out-of-pocket cost. Depending on your redemption needs, you may not need to purchase miles at all . Hot Tip: For more ways to use your miles, read our dedicated guide on our favorite ways to redeem Avianca Lifemiles . Final Thoughts While there are plenty of ways to earn Avianca LifeMiles , you may still find yourself just short of the miles needed for a specific redemption. In that case, buying a small number of miles through this promotion could help you book your award sooner. If you plan to buy Lifemiles at 1.43 cents each, make sure to do so before July 24.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Star analyst Dan Ives forms Yorkville Ives merchant bank after leaving Wedbush\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/star-analyst-dan-ives-forms-yorkville-ives-merchant-bank-after-leaving-wedbush.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Fstar-analyst-dan-ives-forms-yorkville-ives-merchant-bank-after-leaving-wedbush.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T14:24:47.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The new firm, Yorkville Ives & Co., will combine investment banking, equity research, institutional trading and principal investing.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"The Chase Sapphire Preferred Card’s 100,000-Point Welcome Offer Is Ending Soon\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/chase-sapphire-preferred-card-100k-bonus-ending-soon/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Chase-Sapphire-Preferred-Gray-Marble-Background-Upgraded-Points-LLC-2.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T14:15:50.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The best-ever welcome offer on the Chase Sapphire Preferred® Card is officially ending soon, and there are just a couple of weeks left to take advantage. While we don’t yet know the exact end date, we have confirmed the offer will end soon. If you’ve been thinking about applying, here’s what you need to know before the window closes. Chase Sapphire Preferred Card’s 100K Welcome Offer Right now, eligible new applicants for the Chase Sapphire Preferred card can earn 100,000 bonus Chase Ultimate Rewards points after spending $5,000 on purchases in the first 3 months from account opening. This is the best welcome offer the Chase Sapphire Preferred card has ever carried — and it’s only the third time in the card’s history that a 100,000-point bonus has been available . The standard offer sits at 75,000 points, so this is 33% more than what new applicants typically see. We value Chase Ultimate Rewards points at 2 cents apiece, putting this welcome offer at roughly $2,000 in travel value. Transfer points to one of Chase’s many airline or hotel partners , and that figure can climb even higher. Hot Tip: What can you do with these points? Take a look at our guide covering the best ways to redeem Chase Ultimate Rewards points . What’s New for 2026? The timing here is worth paying attention to, because the Chase Sapphire Preferred card received a notable refresh for 2026 — without any increase to its $95 annual fee. New additions include 3x points on gas and EV charging, 3x points on vacation rentals, a $120 application fee credit for Global Entry, TSA PreCheck, or NEXUS , and an enhanced Chase Travel hotel credit now worth up to $100 annually , doubled from the previous $50. There is one significant downside, though. New Chase Sapphire Preferred cardmembers will face a reduced 4:3 transfer rate to World of Hyatt, while all other travel partners maintain the standard 1:1 ratio. Even so, combined with the card’s existing bonus categories and its lineup of airline and hotel transfer partners, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is as well-rounded as it’s ever been. Starting with 100,000 bonus points on a card this large is a move worth making. Who’s Eligible for the Chase Sapphire Preferred Card? Chase updated its eligibility rules for the Sapphire family of cards in 2025, and the most important change is that you can only earn a welcome bonus offer on each Sapphire card once per lifetime . If you’ve already earned a Chase Sapphire Preferred card welcome offer at any point in the past, you won’t qualify for this one. That said, the updated rules have also opened a new door for some applicants. If you currently hold the Chase Sapphire Reserve® or Sapphire Reserve for Business℠ and have never earned a welcome offer specifically on the Chase Sapphire Preferred card, you may now be eligible to apply — something that wasn’t possible under Chase’s older eligibility rules. The Chase Sapphire card eligibility rules look a little different in 2026. Image Credit: Upgraded Points Beyond Sapphire-specific requirements, you’ll also need to be under Chase’s 5/24 threshold — meaning you’ve opened fewer than 5 new credit cards across all issuers in the past 24 months — and have good to excellent credit. » Related: Applying for Credit Cards: Rules for Each Bank [Limits, Bonus Eligibility, and More] Is The 100K Welcome Offer Worth It? At $95 per year, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card doesn’t have many rivals . The Capital One Venture Rewards Credit Card also has a $95 annual fee, but is currently offering a 75,000-mile welcome bonus offer — 25,000 points short of what the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is offering right now. The American Express® Gold Card ‘s offer can reach as high as 100,000 points, but its $325 annual fee is much higher ( rates & fees ). Final Thoughts If you’re eligible and have been weighing the Chase Sapphire Preferred card , there’s not much reason to hold off. Once this bonus offer is gone, there’s no guarantee it will come back. The combination of a 100,000-point welcome offer, a modest annual fee, and access to one of the most flexible rewards currencies in travel is rare. This limited-time welcome offer has appeared only twice in the card’s 17-year history. Since it’s going away soon, it’s worth taking a closer look while you still can.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Earn 50% Bonus TAP Miles on Business Class Flights to Europe [Book by July 26]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/tap-air-portugal-bonus-miles/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/TAP-Air-Portugal-Airbus-A339neo-at-Lisbon-Airport-LIS.jpeg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T14:11:09.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"For a limited time, Portuguese national flag carrier TAP is offering a 50% miles bonus on business class flights between the U.S., Canada, or Brazil and Europe. This booking window for this offer is through July 26, 2026, and is valid for travel until August 31, 2026 , so you’ll have to move quickly if you want to get these bonus miles. Here are the details. How To Earn 50% More TAP Miles To earn the bonus, simply book an eligible business class cash ticket by July 26 for travel through August 31 between the U.S., Canada, or Brazil and Europe , then add your TAP Air Portugal Miles&Go frequent flyer account number to your reservation. You’ll automatically receive the 50% bonus miles. The promotion’s terms don’t list any blackout dates or required travel periods. That means all eligible flights booked by July 26 should qualify . Travelers can expect the bonus miles earned through the promotion to be credited to their Miles&Go accounts within 15 days of the standard miles being credited. The coveted throne seat on TAP’s Airbus A321LR. Image Credit: Daniel Ross Bonus miles will expire 1 year from the date that they are credited. Is This a Good Deal? While a 50% bonus is certainly generous , we’d suggest doing some math before you go ahead and book a business class flight with TAP to earn these bonus miles. For example, let’s say you were planning a trip to Portugal or elsewhere in Europe . If booking TAP is a viable option for your trip, then earning 50% bonus miles to put toward your next trip is certainly a great incentive to take advantage of this offer. However, we wouldn’t advise booking with TAP purely to take advantage of the 50% bonus miles offer if another airline is cheaper or offers a more direct route. Hot Tip: If you frequently fly with TAP and wish to earn more miles through TAP’s Miles&Go program for flights to Europe, you might want to think about applying for the TAP Miles&Go American Express® Card from Cardless . Final Thoughts If you’re planning a business class trip between Europe and the U.S., Canada, or Brazil, TAP’s current offer could help you earn 50% more Miles&Go miles along the way. Be sure to compare airfare with other airlines beforehand. If the TAP options suit your needs, be sure to book the business class cash ticket promptly, as this bonus miles offer ends on July 26.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=19832390\",\"feedTitle\":\"Asia News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Ex-Fed advisor gets over three years in prison for lying about China ties\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/16/ex-fed-adviser-gets-jailtime-lying-about-china-ties-economic-espionage-.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F16%2Fex-fed-adviser-gets-jailtime-lying-about-china-ties-economic-espionage-.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T14:09:32.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The case marks one of the most prominent U.S. prosecutions alleging Chinese intelligence targeting of U.S. institutions, as Trump intensifies its pursuit of foreign economic espionage.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSWorldNews\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: World News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Iran Allows U.S. Citizen It Held for More Than a Year to Leave\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/iran-allows-u-s-citizen-it-held-for-more-than-a-year-to-leave-035b44e0\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-27156117\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T14:02:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Handout\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"United and Lufthansa’s Top Elite Members Will Soon Enjoy New Reciprocal Perks\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/united-lufthansa-reciprocal-perks-elites/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/United-737-Max-9-taxiing-LAX-American-Airlines.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:51:18.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"If you hold United Global Services or Lufthansa HON Circle status, you’ll soon have a few more perks to look forward to. Starting July 22, the 2 airlines are rolling out new reciprocal benefits that give their most loyal flyers additional recognition and perks when traveling on participating transatlantic partner airlines. Here’s what eligible travelers can expect. New Perks for United and Lufthansa’s Top-Tier Elites The new reciprocal benefits are reserved for each airline’s highest-tier elite members. That means United Global Services — the airline’s invitation-only status for its most valuable customers — and Lufthansa HON Circle , which is reserved for the carrier’s most frequent premium cabin travelers. Starting July 22 , United Global Services members flying with Lufthansa Group airlines — including Lufthansa , SWISS , Austrian Airlines , Brussels Airlines, Discover Airlines, and Lufthansa City Airlines — will receive additional recognition throughout their journey. The same goes for Lufthansa HON Circle members when flying with United . Neither airline has shared a full list of benefits yet, but eligible travelers can expect things like preferred seat selection, enhanced recognition at the airport, and extra support during delays or other travel disruptions . New perks are coming for United’s top-tier elites flying Lufthansa partners. Image Credit: Daniel Ross These new benefits are designed to complement — not replace — the reciprocal perks that travelers already receive through Star Alliance . Instead, they make flying with a partner airline a little more seamless for each airline’s most loyal customers. That said, the experience won’t be identical across every airline. Each participating carrier will provide its own set of perks rather than offering a standardized list of benefits. United also says that additional airlines in its Atlantic joint venture — a partnership between several airlines that work together on flights between North America and Europe — could join the program in the future. For now, though, it hasn’t announced which carriers could be added or when the program might expand. Hot Tip: This new reciprocal program is only available to United Global Services and Lufthansa HON Circle members. It does not apply to United Premier members , Lufthansa Miles & More Senator members, or other Star Alliance elite tiers. Final Thoughts For most travelers, this announcement won’t change much. But for United and Lufthansa’s most loyal customers, it should make flying between the airlines feel a little more seamless. While many of the details are still under wraps, added recognition, better seat selection opportunities, and extra support during travel disruptions could help create a more consistent premium experience across both carriers.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSWorldNews\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: World News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Trump Has Threatened to Bomb Iran’s Pickaxe Mountain. What Is Hidden There?\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/trump-has-threatened-to-bomb-irans-pickaxe-mountain-what-is-hidden-there-b1d96dfb\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-56098335\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:50:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Vantor/Reuters\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/302.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Cryptocurrency Opinion & Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Ethereum ETF Inflows Strengthen the Case for a Break Above $1,900\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/ethereum-etf-inflows-strengthen-the-case-for-a-break-above-1900-200684061\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fethereum-etf-inflows-strengthen-the-case-for-a-break-above-1900-200684061&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:46:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"New Accor Live Limitless Promotion: Up to 7,500 Points per Stay, Plus Other Limited-Time Offers\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/accor-points-promo/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Banyan-Tree-Mayakoba.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:40:49.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Accor has numerous promotions to help you earn bonus points at select hotels worldwide. Whether you’re booking a business trip or just heading on a fun trip to somewhere new, there’s a chance you can earn bonus points along the way. Depending on where you’re traveling and the length of your stay, you can earn up to 7,500 points on stays this summer. That’s on top of ongoing offers for 2x and 4 points. Let’s take a look at all of Accor’s ongoing promotions and how you can use them to earn more on your next stay. Up to 7,500 Bonus Points in Europe and Western Asia Accor Live Limitless members can earn up to 7,500 bonus points per stay in what the chain is calling a “Europe and beyond” promotion . Along with European countries, this offer applies to western Asia and some French overseas territories like Mayotte and French Guiana, among others. Image Credit: Accor Guests need to book by July 31 and complete their stays by September 13, 2026 , to earn bonus points with this offer. The number of points you’ll earn depends on the length of stay and whether you have an Accor+ membership : ALL members: 1,000 bonus points on stays of 2-4 nights, 5,000 bonus points on stays of 5+ nights Accor+ members:: 1,500 bonus points on stays of 2-4 nights, 7,500 bonus points on stays of 5+ nights Up to 4x Points at Lifestyle and All-Inclusive Properties Guests can earn up to 4x points at select brands in multiple parts of the world, but this bonus is only available once per member . Registration is required, and the 4x earnings don’t apply in Europe or the Americas. There, the promotion offers 3x points. Members can save 20% or more on their next stay, plus earn 3x or 4x points. Participating Accor brands for this offer include Mama Shelter, The Hoxton, 25hours, SLS, SO/, Mondrian, Hyde, Delano, Banyan Tree, Rixos, Faena, and 21C. Booking deadlines vary by destination, but eligible stay dates are July 3 to September 7, 2026 . Image Credit: Accor Booking deadlines are as follows: Lifestyle hotels in Americas and Europe: Book by June 17, 2026 Lifestyle hotels in the Middle East and Asia Pacific: Book by July 31, 2026 All inclusive hotels worldwide: Book by July 31, 2026 2x Points on Summer Stays Across the Americas This new promotion offers 2x points at participating hotels in Canada, the U.S., Mexico, the Caribbean, Panama, and Brazil . Just make sure you register here and book by August 8 . Eligible stays must be completed by September 8, 2026 . Image Credit: Accor For example, if you book a stay at a participating hotel such as the Sofitel New York or Faena Hotel Miami Beach, you’ll earn double points. 4x Points at New Accor Hotels If there’s a new Accor property at your destination, you can earn 4x points by staying there. However, only reservations made after registration qualify. The list of properties and eligible dates are updated every 60 days. This offer applies to bookings made by August 2 for stays through November 29, 2026 . The full list of participating properties includes over 30 hotels, with destinations including the U.S., Belgium, China, France, Japan, and more. Double Points for Events in the Americas Those who book meetings and events with Accor can earn double points on these through December 31, 2026 . Points will be deposited in your account within a month of the event, and you must register for this offer before your event. 100 Bonus for Enabling WhatsApp Notifications If you enable WhatsApp notifications for the first time, you’ll earn 100 bonus points. There’s no end date listed for this offer , and you can only earn the bonus once. [Booking Closed] 4x Points in Select Regions Guests who book by May 3 and stay by August 31, 2026, can earn up to 3x points on their stays. Stays of 1 or 2 nights earn 2x points, while stays of 3 nights or more earn 3x points. Registration is required for this offer . Image Credit: Accor This promotion it applies to stays in the following countries : Australia, Bahrain, Benin, Botswana, Cambodia, Cameroon, Democratic Republic Of Congo, Egypt, Equatorial Guinea, Fiji Islands, French Polynesia, Ghana, India, Indonesia, Iraq, Ivory Coast, Japan, Jordan, Kenya, Kuwait, Lao people’s democratic republic, Lebanon, Madagascar, Malaysia, Maldives, Mauritania, Mauritius, Myanmar, Namibia, New Zealand, Nigeria, Oman, Pakistan, Philippines, Qatar, Rwanda, St Helena, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, Seychelles, Singapore, South Africa, South Korea, Sri Lanka, Tanzania, Thailand, Turkey, United Arab Emirates, Vietnam, and Zimbabwe. Earning and Burning ALL Points ALL – Accor Live Limitless Reward points have a unique structure. Points can be redeemed for discounts on your statement when you stay at Accor properties. You can redeem them in increments of 2,000 points; every 2,000 points you redeem will get you €40 (~$46) towards a stay . You can earn ALL Reward points in a wide variety of ways. Check out our guide that covers the best ways to earn ALL – All Live Limitless Reward points to save big on your next stay. Hot Tip: Looking for inspiration for where to use your ALL points? Check out the best Ennismore properties in the world , including SLS Hotels & Residences, Mondrian, Delano, The Redbury, and Hyde Hotels & Residences. Final Thoughts Accor’s latest round of promotions — including up to 4x points at participating brands and up to 7,500 points in multiple countries — creates an easy opportunity to boost your ALL balance if you have paid stays coming up. And with several other offers running at the same time, it’s worth checking what you’re eligible for before you book.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"How I Used 100K Chase Sapphire Preferred Points for a Trip to Thailand\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/chase-sapphire-preferred-100k-bonus-thailand/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Chase-Sapphire-Preferred-Card-Beach-Upgraded-Points-LLC.webp\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:30:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The Chase Sapphire Preferred ® Card has been a mainstay in my wallet, and thanks to the card’s recent refresh, I actually find it much easier to earn rewards on frequent, everyday purchases. I’ve had this card for a few years now, and my strategy for rewards has always been to accrue a large pile, then take a big trip. Here’s how I used 100,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points for a trip to my favorite country in the world: Thailand. Chase Sapphire Preferred Card Overview The Chase Sapphire Preferred card recently had a benefits refresh , now offering perks such as a $100 hotel credit in Chase Travel (an easy way to offset the $95 annual fee), a complimentary 1-year Apple TV+ subscription (if activated by December 31, 2026), and up to a $120 credit for Global Entry, TSA PreCheck, or NEXUS every 4 years. Thanks to refreshed bonus earning categories, I now earn the following: 5x points on all travel booked via the Chase Travel portal 3x points on dining purchases, online grocery purchases (excluding Walmart, Target, and wholesale clubs), gas and EV charging, vacation homes (such as Airbnb and Vrbo), and some streaming services 2x points on all other travel worldwide 1x points on everything else I can rack up a lot of points with everyday spending on the card , including eating out, online grocery shopping, gas, and streaming. However, if you don’t yet have the card, the Chase Sapphire Preferred card has a rare, higher-than-usual welcome offer right now: Earn 75,000 100,000 points after spending $5,000 on purchases in the first 3 months. There’s a lot you can do with 100,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points , like a vacation to Europe . I used them to take a points-fueled trip to one of my favorite destinations, Thailand. » Related: How Much Are 100K Chase Ultimate Rewards Points Worth? Redeeming 100K Points for a Trip to Thailand Although you might be able to get round-trip tickets to Thailand or a longer hotel stay, I used my points for a one-way flight to Bangkok from the U.S. and a few nights in a hotel in Bangkok . Flights to Bangkok I flew Qatar Airways from Atlanta (ATL) to Bangkok (BKK), with cash prices hovering around $1,200 one-way on my chosen dates. After searching on their website, I found various dates with award availability that cost 47,500 Qatar Avios one-way with a layover in Doha (DOH), less than half the current welcome offer of 100,000 points . Qatar Avios rates for one-way flights between Atlanta (ATL) and Bangkok (BKK). Image Credit: Qatar Airways One important thing to note is that Qatar Airways isn’t actually a transfer partner of Chase — but there was a workaround that turned my Chase points into Qatar Avios . British Airways is a Chase transfer partner , so I was able to transfer 48,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points to British Airways Avios at a 1:1 ratio . Then, because I had previously connected my British Airways Avios and Qatar Airways Avios accounts, I was able to move the points from BA to Qatar using the transfer tool on Avios.com at a 1:1 ratio, so I ended up with Qatar Airways Avios and was then able to book my ticket, spending 47,500 Avios and about $150 in taxes and fees. If I have to fly economy, Qatar isn’t a bad choice, especially if I’m paying (mostly) with Avios. Image Credit: Keri Stooksbury We value Chase Ultimate Rewards points at about 2 cents per point, so I estimate that, after subtracting taxes and fees from the $1,200 cash price, I got about 2.2 cents per point in value, slightly more than the Upgraded Points valuation. Plus, we value British Airways Avios and Qatar Airways Avios at 1.25 cents per point, so if you look at it from that angle, I got a great deal. Will I be flying for about 20 hours in small economy plane seats? Yes. But considering my flight was nearly free, I don’t mind smushing into a small economy seat and saving my cash for mango sticky rice and tuk-tuk rides in Bangkok. Hot Tip: You can now move Avios among Aer Lingus AerClub, British Airways Club, Finnair Plus, Club Iberia Plus, Loganair Loyalty, Qatar Airways Privilege Club, and Vueling Club accounts for free and instantly, as long as the account name matches at each airline. Hotels in Bangkok After purchasing my flight, I was left with 52,000 Chase points, enough for a 4-night stay at the Hyatt Regency Bangkok Sukhumvit , which has an outdoor pool, 24-hour-a-day fitness center, and easy, direct access to the Nana BTS station. The price was 12,000 Hyatt points per night (or $256 in cash per night). Points rates at the Hyatt Regency Bangkok Sukhumvit. Image Credit: Hyatt I applied for and was approved for my Chase Sapphire Preferred card before June 15, 2026, which means I can still transfer Chase Ultimate Rewards points to Hyatt points at a 1:1 ratio until October 1, 2026 . Unfortunately, after the card’s most recent refresh, new Chase Sapphire Preferred card members (and all cardholders after October 1, 2026) have a transfer ratio of 4:3 , meaning those Chase points are worth about 25% less when moved to Hyatt . This means that to book a Hyatt hotel costing 12,000 points per night, you’d have to transfer 16,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points to Hyatt for the redemption. In this situation, I would only have been able to afford 3 nights with my leftover Chase Ultimate Rewards points, or I would have had to consider a more affordable hotel if I wanted to stay longer. This is a real bummer, because Hyatt was one of my favorite Chase transfer partners. Cash rates at the Hyatt Regency Bangkok Sukhumvit. Image Credit: Hyatt We value Hyatt points at 1.4 cents per point, and given the cash rates of $256 per night, I was able to get a value of 2.1 cents per point (still more than we value Chase points at, which is 2 cents per point). The good news is that since I was grandfathered into the former Chase-Hyatt 1:1 transfer ratio, I still had a few thousand Chase Ultimate Rewards points left in my account for my next trip. Stay at properties like the Hyatt Place Bangkok Sukhumvit for as low as 4,500 Hyatt points per night. Image Credit: Hyatt If you’re hoping to get as many hotel nights as possible out of your Chase Ultimate Rewards Points, there are a few Hyatt-branded properties in Thailand, such as the Hyatt Place Bangkok Sukhumvit , that cost just 4,500 Hyatt points per night. Not a bad Bangkok pool for 4,500 Hyatt points per night. Image Credit: Ehsan Haque Even if you’re only getting 75% of the points after the transfer, you can still get value. Just make sure to check cash prices and do the math to ensure it’s a good deal. » Related: Chase Sapphire Preferred’s Welcome Bonus Offer History: 2020 to 2026 Booking the Rest of My Thailand Trip It’s true that 100,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points didn’t get me an entire trip to Thailand for free, but it did significantly lower the cost of a vacation to a destination that’s really far from the U.S. and expensive to reach. That’s why I combine my Ultimate Rewards points with other card perks and rewards. In the end, I used the $300 travel credit on my Capital One Venture X Rewards Credit Card to buy flights in Capital One Travel between Bangkok and Koh Samui (USM) and IHG One Rewards points to pay for the Holiday Inn Bophut Beach Resort on the island, earned on my IHG One Rewards Premier Credit Card . I used American Airlines miles (transferred from Citi ThankYou Points earned on my Citi Strata Elite℠ Card ) to fly Qatar Airways home from Bangkok, with a stop in Doha (DOH). Using points and miles, largely earned with my Chase Sapphire Preferred card, enabled me to take a dream trip to Thailand I might not have been able to afford otherwise. Hot Tip: There are many ways to use 100,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points, from incredible first-class flights to getting to Hawaii or Europe . We even recorded a podcast to share all the best redemptions with you. Final Thoughts If you don’t already have the Chase Sapphire Preferred card , now is the time to apply with the elevated welcome bonus offer. 100,000 points could land you a flight and a few nights of hotel in a dream destination in Thailand. If you already have the card, you could follow my strategy and save up as many points as possible and transfer them to Hyatt before October 1. However, only do this if you have a redemption in mind, such as a stay in Thailand.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/302.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Cryptocurrency Opinion & Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"ETH/BTC Breakout Signals Growing Altcoin Strength, but Bitcoin Recovery Stays Key\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/ethbtc-breakout-signals-growing-altcoin-strength-but-bitcoin-recovery-stays-key-200684058\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fethbtc-breakout-signals-growing-altcoin-strength-but-bitcoin-recovery-stays-key-200684058&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:28:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Southwest Airlines Schedule Extended Through April 2027\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/southwest-extends-flight-schedule/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Southwest-Airlines-airplane-wing-over-Chicago.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:21:28.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Southwest Airlines has extended its flight schedule, and you can now book Southwest flights for travel through April 5, 2027 . Here are the details you’ll need to book those spring flights that you’ve had your eye on but couldn’t book until now. Southwest Airlines Releases Schedule Through April 2027 Southwest Airlines has released its flight schedule through April 5, 2027 , so it’s time to book that spring getaway you’ve been thinking about for the beginning of next year. If you’re unsure where to travel, don’t forget that Southwest flies to many vacation spots, including Hawaii and international destinations like Costa Rica and the Caribbean. Unlike other airlines, which release schedules about 11 months in advance, Southwest releases its schedule in smaller chunks — usually about 8 to 9 months in advance . Southwest has released its flight schedule through April 5, 2027. Image Credit: Southwest Airlines Why is this so important, you might ask? Flights tend to increase in price as you get closer to your desired travel dates, so you can often save money by booking flights as soon as they’re released . Since Southwest doesn’t charge change or cancellation fees, there’s no downside to booking early . If you book your flight with Rapid Rewards points and the price drops, you can change your flight to the lower-priced option and get a points refund. Southwest offers several  fare classes, which were recently updated . For instance, if you booked a Basic or Choice fare with cash, you can get a flight credit for the price difference. If you book a Choice Preferred or Choice Extra ticket, your fare is fully refundable, whether you paid with points or cash. Hot Tip: With all of the changes at the airline, you now have ability to choose an assigned seat , based on fare class, elite status, and whether or not you have a Southwest credit card . When Will the Southwest Schedule Be Extended? Southwest Airlines releases its flight schedule in small chunks throughout the year. Flights are currently available to book through April 5, 2027. On August 27 2026, Southwest plans to extend the schedule through June 2, 2027. Final Thoughts Southwest Airlines doesn’t release a flight schedule in the same manner as other airlines. Instead, it opts for small chunks of flights released throughout the year. If you’ve been eyeing a Southwest flight for travel plans at the beginning of next year, you can now reserve travel through April 5, 2027, thanks to the airline extending its schedule.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort Review: A Laid-Back Hawaiian Getaway\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/travel/hotels/sheraton-kauai-coconut-beach-resort-review/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Sheraton-Kauai-Coconut-Beach-Resort-pool-and-beach.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T13:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The author was a guest of Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort. All opinions are the author’s own, and neither Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort nor its parent company had input in any part of this article. My daughter and I spent 3 nights at the Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort in June 2026 in order to do the “hard work” of writing this review. Choosing a hotel in Hawaii can be overwhelming, so hopefully, this will help you narrow your choices, especially if you are looking for a Kauai hotel that can be booked with Marriott Bonvoy points. Overall, this is a low-key, small-ish hotel. If you’re looking for a massive resort complex, look elsewhere. But if you want a solid beachfront resort with a nice pool, ocean views, and some good food that won’t break the bank, Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort could easily fit the bill. Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort Overview Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort is a laid-back Hawaiian resort with just 314 rooms. The pool is at the center of the property, and it’s easy to reach from any room. I could get from my room to the pool in under 2 minutes. It isn’t one of those sprawling resorts that require a map and a golf cart to navigate. I found it to be a low-key oceanfront property, better suited to a quiet stay. The pool is the focal point of the resort. Hot Tip: Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort underwent an extensive $35 million renovation in 2019 and has 13 oceanfront king suites undergoing renovations, which are expected to debut in mid-August 2026 . Marriott Hotels on Kauai There are 8 Marriott hotels on the island of Kauai , including 2 Sheratons, a Sheraton Vacation Club, a Westin Vacation Club, 3 Marriott Vacation Clubs, and an Autograph Collection property. Be sure not to confuse Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort with Sheraton Kauai Resort or Sheraton Kauai Resort Villas — they are different properties. Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort is on the east side of the island, just over 6 miles north of Lihue Airport (LIH). It was easy to grab an Uber at the airport for the quick 12- to 15-minute drive to the resort. The other 2 Sheratons on the island are on the south side in Poipu. » Related: The 9 Best Hawaii Hotels To Book With Points [For Max Value] Booking Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort Base-level rooms during my stay at Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort started at $502 , including taxes and fees, or 72,000 Marriott Bonvoy points per night. The room I stayed in, a Deluxe Oceanfront Queen, starts at around $683 per night. There was a $45 resort fee per night , even when booking with points. The resort fee included: Welcome drink and lei upon arrival for 2 guests per stay Daily 2-hour cruiser bike rental for 2 guests Beach chair and umbrella rental for 2 guests Daily resort activities (morning yoga, lawn games, hula lessons, ukulele lessons, lei-making classes, etc.) for 2 guests Daily action camera rental with accessories and equipment Deluxe arcade room access for 2 people Daily enhanced high-speed internet access While $500 per night isn’t cheap, it’s a moderate price for a resort on Kauai. This resort was featured on our “Hawaii Hotels — Splurge vs. Steal” podcast episode as a steal for Kauai. Hot Tip: Need more Marriott Bonvoy points? You can earn them by using a Marriott-branded credit card , or by transferring them from Chase Ultimate Rewards , American Express Membership Rewards , or Bilt Rewards . Deluxe Oceanfront Queen Room We spent 3 nights in a Deluxe Oceanfront Queen Room. It had a spectacular oceanfront location and a private balcony for enjoying the views. Since we were facing east, it was a perfect spot to watch the sunrise with a cup of coffee. The room was a spacious 672 square feet with 2 queen beds. The decor was minimalist yet fresh and tropical, with a large-scale wave mural behind the beds that added color and whimsy. There was also a set of drawers, a coffee maker, and a separate sitting area. The bathroom featured double sinks and a spacious shower with a bench. I enjoyed the Gilchrist & Soames Warm Oak bath products and plush robes. Pools and Beach There was 1 main pool at Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort, along with an attached shallow pool for kids and a large hot tub. While 1 pool might not seem like much, it was rarely crowded since this isn’t a huge resort. While the resort is beachfront, there weren’t any chairs set up on the beach. However, there were a few beach chairs and hammocks in the grass near the beach. The water was rough when I visited, and most guests opted for the pool instead of the beach. Food and Beverages The food options were solid for a 3-night trip, but could be repetitive for a longer visit. Each morning, I grabbed coffee for myself and a smoothie for my daughter at First Light Coffee and Juice Bar. Open every morning, this spot served Starbucks coffee and some light breakfast bites. Later each morning, we ate breakfast at Daybreak Restaurant . While a buffet was available, I opted for the à la carte menu. I had planned to try different things each day, but the avocado toast I ordered on the first morning was so delicious that I stuck with it for the rest of my stay. Lunch was by the pool each day. I appreciated the easy QR code ordering system — no trying to flag someone down to take our order. I ordered from my phone, and our food and drinks were brought directly to our poolside seats. Thumbs up for easy poolside ordering. After lunch, we indulged in complimentary poolside shave ice  from 1 to 3 p.m. each day. On our first night, we ate an early dinner (thanks to jet lag) at The Crooked Surf , the pool bar and grill. We attended the luau on our second night and ordered pizza through Uber Eats (at my 12-year-old’s request) on our last night, so I never ate at the resort’s main dinner restaurant, Moa Moa . Resort Activities The resort fee at Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort included lei making, ukulele and hula lessons, crafts, lawn games, bike rentals, and yoga . Some of these activities required advance registration but were complimentary for resort guests. We tried lei making, a shell picture-frame craft, and a ukulele lesson during our stay. We made fresh flower leis. Crafting seashell picture frames. Hot Tip: Coconut Marketplace , an open-air shopping center with special events, live entertainment, and shopping, is less than a 10-minute walk down the beach from the resort. Luau Ka Hikina Attending a Hawaiian luau may be touristy, but I found it worthwhile. The Luau Ka Hikina at Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort happens at 5:30 p.m., 2 to 4 days a week, depending on the season. Admission included a full buffet, open bar, and a show. The luau took place in an open-air event space next to the hotel. While the structure took away a bit of the ambiance of being outside in Hawaii, I appreciated that the weather was less of a concern. I’ve been disappointed by a rainout at a luau. The show, which explored Hawaiian and Polynesian culture through song and dance, was excellent. I had a smile on my face the entire evening. As of July 2026, adult tickets cost $193.75, kids from 7 to 13 cost $130.64, and kids 3 to 6 cost $88.57. Final Thoughts I enjoyed my 3-night stay at Sheraton Kauai Coconut Beach Resort . It’s a small resort with 1 main pool and limited dining options, but I enjoyed its beachfront location, large hot tub, and luau. Whether booking with Marriott Bonvoy points or cash, it’s a moderately priced Hawaiian resort.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10001147\",\"feedTitle\":\"Business News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"United earnings top estimates but airline expects $6 billion in added fuel costs\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/united-airlines-ual-2q-2026-earnings.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Funited-airlines-ual-2q-2026-earnings.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-16T12:13:49.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"United report