h.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Fed Chairman Kevin Warsh's testimony to Senate banking committee hits on economy, interest rates\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/watch-fed-chairman-kevin-warsh-testify-live-before-senate-banking-committee.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Fwatch-fed-chairman-kevin-warsh-testify-live-before-senate-banking-committee.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T22:05:14.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"As part of congressionally mandated Capitol Hill appearances for the central bank leader, Warsh spoke Tuesday to the House financial services committee.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/286.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Most Popular Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"SpaceX Falls Below Its IPO Price, But Credit Is Sending the Real Warning\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/spacex-falls-below-its-ipo-price-but-credit-is-sending-the-real-warning-200684008\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fspacex-falls-below-its-ipo-price-but-credit-is-sending-the-real-warning-200684008&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T20:42:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"First Look at the New Chase Sapphire Lounge in Dallas\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/chase-sapphire-lounge-dallas-dfw-first-look/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Chase-Sapphire-Lounge-Dallas-DFW-fireplace.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T19:50:27.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"There’s a brand-new Chase Sapphire Lounge by The Club at Dallas Fort Worth International Airport (DFW). This 18,000-square-foot space features Texas-inspired decor and food, premium amenities, and the lounge network’s first-ever whiskey bar. This will be the ninth Chase Sapphire Lounge in the U.S. Upgraded Points was invited to a media preview of the lounge on July 15 ahead of its official opening on July 16, 2026. With perks like a Face Haus spa, a family room, a private nursing room, rest pods, and showers, this new lounge will be a relaxing respite for travelers in Dallas. Here’s a first look inside this new Chase Sapphire Lounge. Chase Sapphire Lounge at DFW Airport The new Chase Sapphire Lounge at Dallas Fort Worth International Airport (DFW) officially opens on July 16, 2026. Announced earlier today , the lounge is located in Terminal D by Gate D25 and is open from 5 a.m. to 10 p.m. daily . This 18,000-square-foot lounge draws inspiration from the city and state it calls home. Earth tones, leather, and textured fabric (even faux cow-hide) reflect the Texas landscape, while sleek stones and modern lighting incorporate the modernity of Dallas. Texas-inspired art and photograpby can be found throughout the lounge and is featured over the signature Chase Sapphire Lounge fireplace. The lounge’s signature fireplace is a showcase for a massive photograph of Texas. Bottom Line: The new Chase Sapphire Lounge at DFW airport opens on July 16, 2026. It’s the ninth Chase Sapphire Lounge in the U.S. and includes premium food and drinks, plus amenities including a Face Haus spa, rest pods, and showers. Amenities The Chase Sapphire Lounge in Dallas features lots of different seating types so guests will be comfortable whether they want to grab a drink, gather with friends, dine in, or get some work done. While there aren’t any runway views, there’s seating along a long hallway with views of the terminal below. One of the most premium features found at select Chase Sapphire Lounges is a Face Haus spa . Travelers can book a complimentary 30-minute treatment to get refreshed before a flight. I had the opportunity to try out a facial and can confirm: It’s a special treat for an airport lounge. If you want to use the Face Haus spa, make an appointment as soon as you get into the lounge, as spots can fill up fast. Next to the 2 spa treatment rooms are 2 rest pods , which can be booked in 30-minute increments. Amenities included an eye mask and ear plugs. There are 2 quiet rooms. At the far end of the lounge, there’s a family room with space dedicated to the youngest travelers, as well as a private nursing room for mothers and babies. The bathrooms were dark, done in a mix of marbles and stones. There was plenty of space as well as a baby changing station and complimentary toiletries. Showers were located near the spa and need to be reserved in advance. Just like the regular bathrooms, the shower room was very dark. The lounge has showers. If you need to take an important call, there’s a private phone room available. The phone room is a quiet spot to take a call. Finally, the Chase Sapphire Lounge at DFW features Peloton stretches and meditations for guests to use on their phones or tablets. These were created exclusively for the lounge network and will soon be available in all Chase Sapphire locations. The one thing I thought was lacking was the number of outlets . Many of the seating areas had no place to charge a phone or tablet, which feels like a miss in such a premium lounge. Hot Tip: Even if you’re on a long layover, you can only access Chase Sapphire Lounges within 3 hours of your departure time. Food and Beverage The Chase Sapphire Lounge in Dallas has partnered with local restaurant Encina to create a menu of Texas-inspired fare, including standouts like Blue Corn Butterscotch Pancakes, DFW Sapphire Burger, Slab Bacon and Cheddar Grits, and Southern Pulled Chicken With Apple and Celery Slaw. The lounge’s signature bar lies at the center of the space. It serves a selection of signature cocktails — which can be made without alcohol — beers, and wines in partnership with Parcelle. Any of the signature cocktails could me made alcohol-free. Travelers can enjoy a first for Chase Sapphire Lounges: a whiskey bar . It features a curated selection of Texas whiskeys, including an exclusive custom barrel selection found only in this lounge. There’s even a traveling whiskey cart that offers guided pairings and a featured cocktail. For guests looking for a lower-octane option, there are 2 separate beverage stations featuring coffee, water, and a selection of soft drinks. One of the highlights is the locally roasted coffee from Cherry Coffee , a Fort Worth-based, female-owned coffee shop. Be sure to grab a biscotti or 2 to enjoy with your coffee. Finally, there was a section of to-go options next to the front desk with light bites, beverages, and coffee (which felt very reminiscent of what you might see at a Capital One Lounge ). This was something we usually don’t see in Chase Sapphire Lounges, so this is a huge plus for Dallas travelers. How To Access the Chase Sapphire Lounge in Dallas There are several ways to access the new Chase Sapphire Lounge at DFW. Select cardholders get unlimited visits for themselves and up to 2 guests. Children under 2 are free, and additional guests are $27 each. Chase Sapphire Reserve® Sapphire Reserve for Business℠ J.P. Morgan Reserve Card The Ritz-Carlton Credit Card (not directly open to applicants but attainable through a product change ) Access to Chase Sapphire Lounges is one of the reasons I keep the Chase Sapphire Reserve card. Additionally, anyone who holds a Priority Pass membership (from any credit card) can access a Chase Sapphire Lounge once per year at no extra cost. Guests cost $27 each, and any additional visit by a Priority Pass member costs $75. Entry is allowed up to 3 hours before your flight, and a same-day boarding pass is always required. » Related: The 7+ Best Credit Cards That Get You Priority Pass Lounge Access [2026] Final Thoughts The new Chase Sapphire Lounge in Dallas opens July 16, 2026. This premium space offers a new place for travelers to rest and recharge before their flight from DFW. Premium amenities include a Face Haus spa, showers, and a whiskey bar.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"United Mile Play Promotion Is Back … With a Very Different Look [Ends August 28]\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/united-mile-play-promotion/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/United-a321.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T19:27:32.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"United often runs a promotion known as Mile Play , with the airline awarding MileagePlus miles to select members after they complete activities. Offers vary widely from 1 person to the next. The offer provides free miles for qualifying activities and incentivizes customers to continue to fly with United, engage with its partners, or spend on its credit cards. This time around, fewer people than normal are seeing offers, and offers now include non-travel activities. Here’s what you should know about the latest promotion and how to register. How To Register for United Mile Play First, you’ll need to register for the Mile Play promotion . Once you enter your United MileagePlus loyalty number, you’ll get to see your targeted promotion. Were You Targeted? Unfortunately, not all members are targeted , though there does appear to be a mix of both United elite status members and non-status holders who are eligible for the offer. Having a higher elite status doesn’t necessarily guarantee you’ll be targeted, though the offers seem to be better for some. If you’re not targeted for the promotion, there’s nothing you can do except hope that you can participate next time. Current United Mile Play Offers The number of miles United will award changes depending on your qualification, elite status level, and pattern of flying. These offers are VERY different from what we normally see . Image Credit: United Most of our team isn’t eligible for an offer this time around. Here are some of the offers that our eligible team members are seeing: Earn 26,000 bonus miles if you open a Chase United credit card , link your United and Lyft accounts , and opt in for United emails. Earn 25,700 bonus miles if you open a Chase United credit card, link your United and Lyft accounts, and opt in for mobile notifications from United. Image Credit: United All offers end on August 28, 2026, so you’ll need to register and complete the qualifying transactions before this date to receive the bonus miles. If your activity requires a flight, understand that a qualifying fare is without taxes, so you’ll likely need to pay over these amounts to be eligible. Award flights don’t count for this promotion, and miles earned don’t count toward United elite status. How To Use Bonus MileagePlus Miles There are tons of great ways to redeem the United miles you earn from this promotion, such as: Upgrades on domestic or international flights Seat assignments or Wi-Fi passes United Club memberships and day passes Flights on both United and partner airlines Some of the offers that are circulating are enough for a cheap, free, one-way flight, so certainly don’t overlook this promotion. Hot Tip: If you need to top off your United MileagePlus balance, you also can transfer your Chase Ultimate Rewards points and Bilt Rewards points at a 1:1 ratio.  Final Thoughts This offer presents a curious twist, no longer offering MileagePlus miles for flying but instead rewarding non-flight activities like getting a credit card, receiving emails, or linking your United and Lyft accounts. Remember that offers are highly personalized, and they all expire on August 28.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/286.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Most Popular Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Headwinds and Tailwinds: Minding the Market Weather\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/headwinds-and-tailwinds-minding-the-market-weather-200683961\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fheadwinds-and-tailwinds-minding-the-market-weather-200683961&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T19:01:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10001147\",\"feedTitle\":\"Business News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"The AI boom just found two new winners: Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan Chase\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/14/goldman-sachs-and-jpmorgan-chase-are-emerging-as-ai-winners.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F14%2Fgoldman-sachs-and-jpmorgan-chase-are-emerging-as-ai-winners.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T18:45:53.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan showed that Wall Street is a major beneficiary of the AI boom, with record revenue driven by surging trading and investment banking.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSMarketsMain\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: Markets\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"JPMorgan’s Latest Defense Move Backs Sub Supplier and Philadelphia Shipbuilding\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/finance/jpmorgans-latest-defense-move-backs-sub-supplier-and-philadelphia-shipbuilding-05a0183e?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-04939989\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T18:25:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Carina Johansen/Bloomberg News\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"[Award Alert] Starlux Business Class Award Space to Taiwan From 75K Points\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/award-alert-us-taipei-business-class/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Starlux-A359-First-Class-honeymoon-seats.jpeg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T18:09:25.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"If Taiwan has been sitting on your travel wish list, now could be one of the best times to book. The Taipei-based Starlux Airlines has released an unusually large amount of business class award space between the U.S. and Taipei for early 2027, starting at 75,000 points. Even better, some flights have as many as 4 business class award seats available — something that’s exceptionally rare on a premium transpacific route. Let’s take a look at the details. Starlux Business Class Award Alert Details We’re currently seeing excellent award availability on Starlux Airlines business class to Taipei (TPE) from numerous U.S. cities, including Los Angeles (LAX), Phoenix (PHX), and Seattle (SEA), as first reported by Miles Made Easy . Starlux’ swanky business class on its Airbus A350-900. Image Credit: Ehsan Haque While that’s great on its own, what’s even more surprising is that we’ve found up to 4 business class seats available for some dates between January and May 2027. Travelers looking to visit Taiwan or other parts of Asia can book flights like this one below from Los Angeles to Taipei in April 2027 using points. Image Credit: Alaska Airlines You can book these lie-flat seats through Alaska Airlines Atmos Rewards for as little as 75,000 points and roughly $26 in taxes and fees each way for the Los Angeles and Seattle routes. If flying from Phoenix, you’ll pay a bit more at a rate of 85,000 points one-way. Class: Business Routes: Los Angeles (LAX), Phoenix (PHX), and Seattle (SEA) to Taipei (TPE) Dates: January through May 2027 Rates: From 75,000 Alaska Atmos Rewards points plus $26 in taxes and fees Even if Taipei isn’t your final destination, this is a fantastic way to get to Asia — or fly home from it. Hot Tip: Ready to book your flight? Be sure to read how to spend 72 hours in Taipei ! Best Ways To Book To search for available dates, you can use a tool like Seats.aero , which gives you a big-picture view of award availability across a range of dates. We’re currently seeing availability for up to 4 business class seats on select flights. Image Credit: Seats.aero Redeeming Alaska Atmos Rewards Points  is the best way to book this deal. However,  earning Alaska points  can be difficult. The fastest way to earn Alaska points is by using an  Alaska Airlines credit card , but you can also earn points by shopping through the  Atmos Rewards Shopping portal , dining at restaurants that participate in  Atmos Rewards Dining , or flying with Alaska’s  Oneworld partners . You can also transfer points from  Bilt Rewards  and  Marriott Bonvoy . » Related: Alaska Partners With Premium Taiwanese Airline Starlux Final Thoughts If you’ve been searching for flights to Taiwan or even want to use it as a landing point for a trip to other points in Asia, the award is a great deal to take advantage of. Starlux business class is often very expensive to book with cash, and award availability is notoriously hard to find. If you can travel soon, don’t wait — we don’t expect this award space to last long.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/302.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Cryptocurrency Opinion & Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Bitcoin’s Cycle Hasn’t Died: It’s Changed Authors\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/bitcoins-cycle-hasnt-died-its-changed-authors-200684000\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fbitcoins-cycle-hasnt-died-its-changed-authors-200684000&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T18:05:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"New York Fed President Williams says inflation has peaked, rates 'well positioned'\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/new-york-fed-president-williams-says-inflation-has-peaked-rates-well-positioned.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Fnew-york-fed-president-williams-says-inflation-has-peaked-rates-well-positioned.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T17:31:41.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Williams cited five reasons why he expects the latest price surge has run its course.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Anthropic moves closer to mega-IPO as bankers line up investor meetings\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/anthropic-ipo-banks-investor-meetings.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Fanthropic-ipo-banks-investor-meetings.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T17:22:51.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Anthropic is lining up investor meetings ahead of a potential IPO as soon as October as the AI startup behind looks to beat rival OpenAI to the public markets.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/320.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETF Analysis & Opinion\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"These Water ETFs Could Be Quiet Winners From Infrastructure Spending\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/these-water-etfs-could-be-quiet-winners-from-infrastructure-spending-200683998\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fthese-water-etfs-could-be-quiet-winners-from-infrastructure-spending-200683998&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T16:51:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Stocks making the biggest moves midday: SpaceX, Apple, PayPal, Cava, Progressive, Micron & more\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/stocks-making-the-biggest-moves-midday-spcx-aapl-pypl-cava-pgr-mu.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F15%2Fstocks-making-the-biggest-moves-midday-spcx-aapl-pypl-cava-pgr-mu.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T16:28:53.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"These are the stocks posting the largest moves in midday trading.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"Chase Opens a New Sapphire Lounge in DFW’s Terminal D\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/chase-sapphire-lounge-dfw-opening/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Chase-Sapphire-Lounge-Dallas-DFW-lounge-area.jpg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T16:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Chase has added another Sapphire Lounge to its growing network, and this one lands in a state that takes its hospitality seriously. The new Chase Sapphire Lounge by The Club at Dallas Fort Worth International Airport (DFW) opens today, July 16, 2026, giving travelers a new place to relax before a flight. Chase says the Dallas-Fort Worth area continues to climb as a top destination for its cardmembers, so opening a lounge here is meant to meet those travelers where they already spend their time. Here’s what guests can expect at this new Sapphire outpost. A Look at the New Chase Sapphire Lounge at DFW You’ll find the lounge post-security in Terminal D, near gate D25 . It’s a split-level space spanning 18,000 square feet, with a full bar, a family room, and a private nursing room . Guests can also book rest pods, showers, and Face Haus facials. Peloton stretches and meditations built specifically for the lounge will be available on your phone or tablet, and Dallas gets them first before they roll out across the rest of the network. » Related: First Look at the New Chase Sapphire Lounge in Dallas The design leans into its surroundings , with leather accents, Texas natural elements, and small nods to Dallas sports. The signature bar has a tiered brass canopy and a stone countertop that doubles as a charging station. On the food side, a partnership with Encina — the Bishop Arts District restaurant — brings dishes like blue corn butterscotch pancakes in the morning and slab bacon with cheddar grits in the afternoon . Coffee comes from Cherry Coffee, a women-owned shop in Fort Worth, and the bar pours a wine list from Parcelle with cocktails and beers sourced from Texas producers . The most interesting amenity is the network’s first whiskey lounge , a tucked-away room with a whiskey cart offering guided pairings, a featured cocktail, and a handpicked selection of Texas whiskeys, including a custom barrel exclusive to this location. Lastly, 2 original murals by Dallas artist Kyle Bunting round out the sports-watching space. The lounge will be open from 5 a.m. to 10 p.m. daily . Hot Tip: DFW has been busy on the lounge front lately. Back in March, Plaza Premium Lounge opened 2 new lounges in Terminal D, including a Plaza Premium First location, adding to a terminal that already houses the Capital One Lounge and the Amex Centurion Lounge . Chase’s arrival makes an already lounge-rich terminal even harder to beat. Check out our guide to all of the DFW lounges . How To Access Chase Sapphire Lounges Access to the Chase Sapphire Lounge by The Club network is tied to a handful of premium cards . Primary cardmembers and authorized users of the Chase Sapphire Reserve® , Sapphire Reserve for Business℠ , J.P. Morgan Reserve Card, and The Ritz-Carlton Credit Card all get in as many times as they want — and at no charge. Cardmembers can bring up to 2 guests per visit at no charge; additional guests cost $27 each, and children under 2 get in free. If you don’t hold one of those cards, there’s still a way to get in. Travelers with a Priority Pass membership issued by another credit card receive 1 complimentary visit to a U.S. Chase Lounge each calendar year. After that, a $75 per-visit fee applies, and additional guests over the age of 2 cost $27 each. » Related: The Best Credit Cards for Airport Lounge Access [2026] Final Thoughts DFW keeps stacking up lounge options, and the new Chase Sapphire Lounge by The Club is a strong addition for anyone flying through Terminal D. Between the Texas-focused food, the whiskey lounge, and the wellness amenities, there’s plenty here to make an early arrival worthwhile. And with a Chase Sapphire Lounge planned for Los Angeles (LAX) within the next year, the network isn’t done growing.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://www.investing.com/rss/320.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETF Analysis & Opinion\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.investing.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"As the Iran War Resumes, 2 Energy ETFs Ride Oil’s Renewed Rally\",\"link\":\"https://www.investing.com/analysis/as-the-iran-war-resumes-2-energy-etfs-ride-oils-renewed-rally-200683990\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.investing.com%2Fanalysis%2Fas-the-iran-war-resumes-2-energy-etfs-ride-oils-renewed-rally-200683990&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dwww.investing.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-15T15:15:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=10000664\",\"feedTitle\":\"Finance\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"Warren Buffett on the market today: 'It's tough to find values when everybody is preferring gambling'\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/15/warren-buffett-on-the-market-today-its-tough-to-find-va